Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Environment Releases 40 Rangers to Search for Missing Helicopter on the Border of Kampong Speu and Pursat Provinces
The director of the Department of Environment confirmed that although the search did not find the missing helicopter, the search team continued to search regularly.
This is the eighth day for the search operation for the helicopter, which has been missing since the evening of July 12, 2024, as the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) combined forces are actively continuing their mission, despite the difficult weather conditions in the area.
It should be noted that on the afternoon of July 12, 2024, a military helicopter lost contact in the Cardamom Mountains while flying training.
General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, confirmed that there were only two people in the helicopter, one pilot and one assistant driver. The floodwaters inundated 20 houses and affected Nearly 50 hectares of irrigated rice in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu provincial governor led professional officers to inspect the situation
(Kampong Speu): The Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, instructed the Department to speed up the opening of the water to facilitate the flow of water when 20 houses were affected in the flood of nearly 50 hectares of rice. Rain.
Immediately after this incident, the Governor of Kampong Speu Province led professional officers and local authorities to inspect the flood situation in Prey Nok Village, Snom Krapeu Commune, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province on the afternoon of July 19, 2024.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan said that due to climate change and this is the rainy season, there has been continuous rain and some lowlands have been inundated.
In Prey Nok village, Snom Krapeu commune, the floodwaters have been attacking rice paddies and houses of many people and many hectares of paddy fields, while also threatening some roads to a village.
The provincial governor said that in order to save rice crops and people's houses from this flood, water resources experts and the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport must cooperate to open the water to allow water to flow from the village to the side. Down quickly for the sake of saving the people's rice in part.
In addition, the Department of Agriculture must be ready to plant rice to provide flood victims with crops damaged by the floods.
On the occasion of inspecting the flood situation in Kong Pisey district, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan also met and talked with the people, in which he reminded people to be more careful about this flood, especially children and the elderly. At the same time, it is necessary to report to the nearest local authority to intervene in the event of an accident in the floods.
