(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia, in collaboration with the Cambodian Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training (MLVT), has launched the inauguration ceremony for the project "Capacity Building and Creating a Supportive Environment. The field of information and communication technology in technical and vocational education and training in Cambodia.
The purpose of this event is to inform stakeholders, including representatives from technical and vocational training institutes in the provinces, cities, relevant ministries and non-governmental organizations about project goals and strategies.
The gathering facilitated discussions on project resources and available support for technical and vocational training institutes focusing on information and communication technology.
This project has four components:
The project is expected to significantly boost the digital skills of young Cambodians by bridging the gap between labor force capacity and labor market needs. By providing ICT graduates on demand, this project will contribute to the overall economic development of Cambodia.
KOICA Cambodia, a bilateral aid agency of the Republic of Korea, has been implementing various development cooperation programs in Cambodia since its Phnom Penh office opened in 2003. Key areas include education, health and rural development. Announcing the appointment of Battambang Provincial Police Commissioner, Brigadier General Danh Eng Bun Chan, replacing Major General Sat Kimsan
(Battambang): The new Commissioner of Battambang Provincial Police was officially inaugurated this morning, July 19, 2024, under the chairmanship of General Sar Thet, National Police Commissioner, on behalf of Mr. Abhisand Bandith Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior. Phay, Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province.
The new Battambang Provincial Police Commissioner to be announced is Brigadier General Danh Eng Bun Chan, replacing retired Major General Sat Kimsan. Brigadier General Danh Eng Bun Chan, before taking office, was the Deputy Commissioner of the Battambang Provincial Police Commissioner for Immigration Planning.
