(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requested Lieutenant General Loeung Tam Quang, Minister of Police of Vietnam, to pardon and release two Cambodians who opened a tourist boat to cross the Vietnamese Sea. To return to Cambodia.
In response, the Vietnamese side agreed to the request, releasing the two Cambodian men.
The request of the Minister of Interior of Cambodia was made during a meeting with the Minister of Police of Vietnam on the afternoon of July 13, 2024. During the meeting, Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requested Lieutenant General Loeung Tam Quang, Minister of Police of Vietnam, to pardon and release the two Cambodian citizens to return to Cambodia.
Based on the results of the talks, especially the cooperation between the two countries, as well as the exchange of information on the security situation and the resolution of various issues along the border, the Vietnamese side agreed to pardon and release the people. The two Cambodians were sent back to the country on the night of July 18, 2024 and through the Prek Chak international border checkpoint in Kampot province, Cambodia.
Meanwhile, immigration officials at the Prek Chak International Border Crossing have returned the two Cambodians to their families.
It should be noted that two Cambodians were arrested by the Vietnamese authorities on April 21, 2024 after driving a tourist boat fishing across the Vietnamese sea.
Chinese, Canadian foreign ministers to meet in Beijing on Friday
The two ministers will discuss regional and global security issues as well as the possibility of cooperating on common challenges.
Relations between China and Canada have been strained since the end of 2018 after a Chinese national was detained in Canada and two Canadians were arrested in China. Although the three were released, Ottawa's allegations of Chinese interference in Canada continued to strain relations.
The visit comes a week after NATO members, including Canada, issued a statement calling China a "major helper" in Russia's war in Ukraine and saying Beijing posed a systemic challenge to Russia. Euro-Atlantic security.
Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Social Affairs: Children are the successor of bamboo, the hope for the nation
(Kampong Thom): Speaking at the 75th Anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 23rd Anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2024, Mr. Chhun Saran, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that children are Bamboo shoots are the hope for the nation.
The day was held on the afternoon of July 18, 2024 under the theme "Investing in Children Today aims to build human capital in the age of digital revolution and jointly implement a commitment to end the worst forms of child labor" on campus. Samrong Primary School, Samrong Village, Samaki Commune, Prasat Balang District, Kampong Thom Province, with the participation of Mr. Vannak Sopheanith, Prasat Balang District Governor, commune authorities, residents, teachers and more than 230 students.
At the same time, he requested the village, commune, district and all stakeholders to continue to coordinate the implementation of the Convention on the Rights of the Child by continuing to promote and strengthen the implementation of legal documents related to the protection of children effectively and transparently.
