IMF raises China's growth forecast for 2024
The International Monetary Fund (IMF) on Tuesday raised China's 2024 economic growth forecast to 5 percent in its latest World Economic Outlook (WEO) report, up from 4.6 percent in the previous month. April. According to the Xinhua news agency.
The rise was due to a recovery in private consumption and strong exports in the first quarter, Xinhua reported, citing the latest report.
"In China, rising domestic consumption boosted positive growth in the first quarter due to a temporary increase in temporary exports compared to rising demand," the report said. The world last year.
The International Monetary Fund (IMF) has maintained its forecast for global growth in 2024 at 3.2 percent, noting that Asia's emerging economies remain a key driver for the global economy.
The current report notes that global activity and world trade increased in late 2023 and early 2024, with trade boosted by strong exports from Asia, especially in the technology sector.
