The Cambodian Human Rights Committee presented the results of a meeting between Senior Minister Keo Remy and the Russian Ambassador to Cambodia, focusing on strengthening human rights cooperation between the two countries.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CPP) has issued a press release on the outcome of a meeting between Senior Minister Keo Remy, President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, and Mr. Anatoly Borovik, Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia on July 18, 2024. The meeting focused on strengthening human rights cooperation between the two countries.
He also mentioned the planned visit of Dr. Tatiana Moskalkova, High Commissioner for Human Rights of the Russian Federation to Cambodia and hoped that the cooperation between Russia and Cambodia in the field of human rights would be improved based on the principles of independence, sovereignty and Non-interference in the internal affairs of other countries.
In addition, the Ambassador highlighted the focus on the promotion and protection of human rights in the Russian Federation, especially on children's rights.
Senior Minister Keo Remy praised the Ambassador for emphasizing the principles set out in the strengthening of cooperation between Russia and Cambodia in the field of human rights and the promotion and protection of children's rights of the Russian Federation.
