His invitation was presented at the Senate on the occasion of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen's courtesy call on the morning of Thursday, July 18, 2024.
The Chinese Ambassador expressed his great pleasure and gratitude for allowing him and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call. He also conveyed greetings from Chinese President Xi Jinping, Chinese Premier Li Jian, Speaker of the National People's Congress and other important leaders.
He said that Samdech Techo was a true old friend of China who supported each other. He also thanked the prince for visiting China during the 19 Kovid eruption, which surprised and fascinated the Chinese people and the world, and considered Samdech Techo a good friend for the people. China, which supports each other in times of emergency. Thus, the well-being of Cambodia is the well-being of China as well.
Samdech Techo also said that Cambodia has maintained this good tradition of friendship since the previous generation of leaders and the care to maintain this relationship to be strong forever. Samdech Techo considered that the historical relationship between the two countries requires our two countries to remain loyal partners.
He recalled that his visit to China at the time of the outbreak of Kovid 19 was a show of solidarity with the Cambodian people and the Chinese people during difficult times and as an encouragement to the Cambodian students who were staying. And continue studying in China. Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo also thanked China for providing 19 Kovid vaccines to Cambodia in a row.
Finally, Samdech Techo also requested the Chinese Ambassador to bring his greetings to Chinese President Xi Jinping and other important Chinese leaders. Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, wished Ambassador Wang Winpin success in his mission in Cambodia.
Tbong Khmum Governor Takes 1,600 Luxury Saplings to Plant at Wat Hong in Hong Natural Waterfall Cave Resort to Promote Environment and Beauty
(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of July 18, 2024, Mr. Pen Kosal, Provincial Governor and Mr. Long Theam, Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Council, led more than 400 government officials, students and citizens to plant 1,600 luxury saplings at Wat Hong Knong. Hoang Barami Waterfall Cave Natural Resort to celebrate (Plant Day July 9) in Chhlong 2 Village, Kampang Commune, Memot District.
Mr. Heng Piseth, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that with the high attention from Mr. Pen Kosal, Provincial Governor, the Department of Agriculture prepared 1,600 luxury saplings in 6 types, including: Kranhong Thnong, Beng Koki Kngok and Cage to plant on 1 hectare at this location to celebrate the 9th of July 2024, 2024.
On that important occasion, Mr. Pen Kosal said that the planting of seedlings in the 9th of July is to reflect the attention of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is actively working on planting and maintenance policies. Reforestation throughout the country and prioritize forest issues to restore and develop the nation.
At the same time, Mr. Pen Kosal said that the choice of this location with careful consideration in order to contribute to the promotion of both the environment and the beauty around here, which is an important natural tourism area for Tbong Khmum.
The provincial governor said that here is a very good potential as a potential eco-tourism resort of the province. Therefore, all relevant departments / units must work together to make this place a tourist attraction.
On that occasion, the provincial governor requested all departments, units, institutions, schools, pagodas, hospitals, as well as all citizens to participate in planting trees and flowers on all roads, especially at home and in public places for Tbong Khmum to become A beautiful area that attracts national and international tourists to visit.
