National Assembly President Khuon Sodary: The Royal Government has a long-term vision to protect religious harmony, peace and development for the people
(Phnom Penh): National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, presides over here this morning July 18, 2024.
As a supporter of Buddhism and a supporter of pure religion, the National Assembly always prepares Preah Vossa candles and offerings to the monks in various temples before the Vesa festival. The Vesa ceremony is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to study the Dharma and Discipline in accordance with the Buddha's teachings for 3 months, starting from the 1st day of the month of Asat. On the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
On the occasion of this festival, Samdech President of the National Assembly met with monks and people in Leuk Dek district with the deepest remembrance on behalf of Samdech led the team to help people in Leuk Dek district from the beginning. . The President of the National Assembly received a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and President of the Senate, and Samdech Moha Bovathipati Hun Manet, Prime Minister.
During the ceremony held at Wat Kiri Ratanaream, also known as Wat Kampong Phnom Knong in Kampong Phnom commune, the National Assembly President thanked the people of Leuk Dek district as well as people across the country who voted overwhelmingly for the Cambodian People's Party on the 23rd. July 2023.
During the ceremony, the monks and the people of Leuk Dek district warmly welcomed the presence of the President of the National Assembly. The people expressed their deepest gratitude to National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, who has always been associated with the people and considered Leuk Dek district as his own hometown, in which he participated in building many achievements for the local people. Raise the iron of both the Buddha and the Empire.
