The professionalism of journalists is protected by law, the law on the press can not protect publishers without respect for ethics and the law.
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the Ministry of Information on the "situation of press freedom in Cambodia", 79.8% of journalists interviewed said that the situation of press freedom in Cambodia is good and 81.8% agree that Respect for ethics and journalism profession is really important.
He noted that 79.80% of the total number of journalists who participated in the 2024 survey on the state of press freedom in Cambodia claimed that "they have complete freedom to pursue a career as a journalist with ease, security and "Independent in gathering information from various sources for writing, producing, publishing their information freely."
The results of this survey are in stark contrast to what some media associations have said about harassment or harassment of journalists, whose reports have not been verified with the relevant authorities' reports. All-round features yet.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Information added that Cambodia now has more than 2,000 media outlets and about 10,000 journalists, both traditional and modern media, who have been carrying out their work, producing and disseminating all forms of information, and Report information freely at all times, safely, gain the trust and support of the public from all walks of life.
Dr. Kin Phea expressed the view that journalists want freedom beyond the law, but it affects the rights of others, so this freedom will be cut off because this affects the rights and freedoms of others. At this point, if the media infringes on the rights of others or affects the security, public order or stability of the state, legal action will be taken against the perpetrators.
"Applying the law to journalists is illegal, not as a restriction on the freedom of the press, but as enforcing the law as part of strengthening the rule of law." This is an additional statement of Dr. Kin Phea.
Dr. points out that the assessment of press freedom in Cambodia by a number of international organizations and a small number of analysts because they focus on a certain angle, so when they focus only on one angle or on the agenda. Whichever one embodies political goals, its assessment is incomplete, which obscures the color of press freedom in Cambodia.
"So any assessment linked to the agenda or political goals, they can not stand on the principle of neutrality and accuracy of the truth of the media situation in Cambodia," Dr. Kin Phea stressed.
Mr. Puy Kea, President of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, said that in a democracy, freedom of expression, some journalists went beyond professionalism and ethics, and this caused some journalists to face legal issues. The veteran journalist also mentioned a number of factors that make journalists punished in terms of the law, including:
First, the journalist did not properly understand what the profession and ethics of the journalist are? Second, he knew, but did not apply it thoroughly, and sometimes the journalist neglected while doing his job. Let them face legal issues and so on.
(Phnom Penh): The Club of Cambodian Journalists, in collaboration with the Insurance Association of Cambodia, on July 18, 2024, organized a forum to share information "on the current state of the insurance market in Cambodia" under the chairmanship of Mr. Bou Chanpirou, Director General of Insurance Regulators in Cambodia. .
The event was also attended by Mr. Puy Kea, President of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, Mr. Huy Ratharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, and about 70 journalists from 58 different institutions at the Fair Hill Bay Hotel. Viet Phnom Penh.
Huy Rataro said the forum not only contributes to strengthening journalists' ability to write articles, but also has a positive and indirect effect on the public through the quality of information.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Bou Chanpirou said that if we talk about a developed country, we need to know the whole financial sector of that country, and when we talk about the financial sector in a country, they talk about three pillars, including: Banking, insurance and securities.
The Director General of the Insurance Regulator in Cambodia said that any country with these three sectors is developing, that country will be a developing country.
Please be informed that the above forum to give journalists the opportunity to learn more about the latest news and developments in the insurance market in Cambodia over the past year to support the writing and promotion of the insurance industry. Hold public effectively and accurately.
The forum also provided an opportunity for journalists to ask questions related to the insurance sector in Cambodia for the speaker to explain and explain more.
(Phnom Penh): The generous gift of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, was handed over by Mr. Seng Teang, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers, on the morning of the 18th. July 2024 at Calmette Hospital.
The generous donations of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit include: 5 million Riel budget, 50 kg of rice, 2 large boxes of milk, 5 kg of sugar, 2 sarongs and 2 scarves.
The triplets, sponsored by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, are the second children in a family of 36-year-old father Toun Virak and 28-year-old mother Chhin Chhorvy, both employed by private companies.
The triplets were born on July 10, 2024 at Calmette Hospital. In front of the family of three twins, Mr. Seng Teang conveyed the deepest condolences from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both of whom always send greetings to the people everywhere. All in Cambodia.
Mr. Seng Teang said that from 1999 to the present, more than 25 years ago, 414 families gave birth to three or four twins and received generous donations from Samdech. Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in supporting the hardships in daily life, especially raising three twin babies, must be Samdech's grandchildren when they give birth.
Mr. Seng Teang continued that all these donations are not gifts from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or the party that serves political activities, instead, all these gifts are gifts from a sincere heart. With the high consideration of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who realized the real difficulties for people giving birth to three or four twin babies.
