(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province and Honorary Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Ratanakkiri Province, stated that the veterans are worthy of the motherland and a symbol of the spirit of self-sacrifice for the nation and a true patriot. No one can be overlooked.
He said this on the morning of July 18, 2024, on the occasion of the 17th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2024, which the Association in cooperation with the provincial administration and the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation organized at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Theater. Invitation from 301 Cambodian Veterans and Relevant Units.
The provincial governor stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia issued Resolution 31 Pillar dated June 20, 2007, designating June 21 as Cambodian Veterans Day, to commemorate the heroism of Cambodian veterans. And to honor the merits of veterans to the nation and the people of Cambodia.
In addition to commemorating the heroism and merits of veterans, this day also aims to spread awareness among the people about veterans, inspire the movement to support veterans, promote the role of veterans in society and promote patriotic spirit at all levels. The people, the armed forces, especially the youth, to turn the youth into worthy pillars and successors with strong ideals, strong and dignified.
Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun supported and evaluated the report and direction for implementation in 2024 and commended the Committee of the Ratanakkiri Veterans Association and related units for their efforts to pay attention to the work of the Royal Government and Management handed over.
