(Kampong Cham): Two red gravel roads in Stung Trang district were inspected and evaluated by two inter-ministerial working groups. Kampong Cham.
The Inter-Ministerial Working Group led by Mr. Pho Pharith, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Chhay Rith Sen, Minister of Rural Development and Rural Road Technical Officer and Representative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on the morning of July 18, 2024, inspected and evaluated the handover. The period of guaranteeing the work of maintaining the anniversary of two roads in Dang Kda and Prek Kak communes, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Ing Visoth, Director of the Department of Rural Development of Kampong Cham Province, said that these two roads are 17.5 kilometers long, 5 meters wide and some roads are 4.5 meters wide, red gravel road, the final stage for the year. 2023, which is a source of funding from the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Department of Rural Development of Kampong Cham Province.
He added that after the inspection and evaluation, the inter-ministerial commission agreed to accept 100% because the committee saw that the two roads were regularly maintained in terms of road length, road size and quantity and quality of roads. One hundred percent good for the benefit of the people in daily use.
After inspecting and evaluating the completion of the two-year road maintenance period, HE Pho Pharith, Secretary of State, Member of the Procurement Committee (SEC), expressed his appreciation to the working group of the Department of Development. Rural, which is the staff of the Ministry in doing a good job, and the commission agreed to accept 100% of the results of the maintenance of the anniversary of the two red gravel roads.
