(Preah Vihear): On the morning of July 18, 2024, Preah Vihear and Champasak provinces of the Lao People's Democratic Republic held a meeting to review the contents of the 10th draft of cooperation between the two provinces on the Cambodia-Laos border in the commune. Kampong Sralao Muy, Chep District, Preah Vihear Province.
The meeting of the Cambodian side "Preah Vihear Province" led by Mr. Nop Vuthy, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, with the participation of the three armed forces, heads of relevant departments around the province, authorities of Chhep district, while the Lao side "Champa Province Tattoo ”led by Mr. Som Buttakun, Deputy Governor and relevant working groups.
On that occasion, Mr. Nop Vuthy sent a message to all Lao delegates from Champasak Province who attended the meeting. Through the Deputy Governor of Champasak Province, Mr. Kim Rithy also sent a message to visit and congratulate the newly appointed Governor of Champasak.
Mr. Nop Vuthy said that the current meeting is focused on reviewing the agreement we signed together last year, how far have we come so far? At the same time, let the team review the new record that Preah Vihear province will host this year.
The Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province told the Lao side that Cambodia has so far had international and regional border crossings, while the traditional border crossings have been closed, but due to the understanding that our two countries have been friends for a long time, we Decided to let our people follow his tradition. However, we are seeking legitimacy in Cambodia-Laos travel as soon as possible.
Mr. Nop Vuthy stated that "Development along the border is the highest priority of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as he always instructs the governors of the border provinces to cooperate between the border provinces." "It is good to do in order to improve the lives of people along the border, so border development is the main direction of the Royal Government."
He added that the cooperation agreement between Preah Vihear and Champasak, which we signed last year, we have implemented very well between the province and the province, district and district, all forces along the border, but we still have Some shortcomings that we need to discuss.
He said that this agreement is that we need to review every year to develop our agreement more deeply. To be removed, to make the border peaceful, to create conditions for our brothers and sisters to live along the border, we have a slogan: "Good brothers, good neighbors must know how to love and respect each other."
