Kampong Cham Provincial Authority Launches Vaccination Campaign for Livestock in Kang Meas District
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of July 18, 2024, led a group of relevant officials to launch a campaign to vaccinate animals from Han disease to farmers in O Kandal village, Prek Krabao commune, Kang Meas district.
The provincial governor said on that occasion that the launch of the vaccination campaign for livestock now is in order to prevent infectious diseases, especially to prevent the spread of smallpox to the livestock of our farmers.
The provincial governor confirmed that raising the livestock of our farmers is not only useful for plowing, they can also benefit from the sale of animal meat.
On the other hand, according to the report of the Department of Agriculture, Kampong Cham has more meat exports than other provinces to sell in the market to supply the needs of the people. Therefore, the supply of meat to the outside to get quality health care, our farmers need to protect the health of animals to make good quality meat does not affect the health of our people who eat.
The provincial governor reminded that last year, for Kang Meas district, there was a problem of animals with waterborne diseases. This year, in Baray commune, Srey Santhor district, there were 7 buffaloes with the disease, but this case was inspected and treated by the veterinary officer of the Provincial Department of Agriculture in time and will be closed at Srey Santhor district has not spread to other areas.
The provincial governor took the opportunity to send a message to all people to take care of their health, because now the weather is changing, causing many diseases that affect the lives of the people. Therefore, people should be protected first by vaccination or living clean and hygienic, and if people are sick, please hurry to consult and treat at the hospital in time.
35 Cambodian students pass scholarship exam to study in Malaysia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and President of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation (CMDF), met with 35 scholarship winners on the afternoon of July 17, 2024 at the Islamic Center in Phnom Penh. PPIC).
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan expressed his happiness and deep gratitude to Dar al-Hikmah University for providing scholarships to Cambodian students so that they have a wider opportunity to strengthen their capacity. It is a great contribution to the development of human resources in Cambodia.
At the same time, Dr. encouraged all students to work hard to learn the knowledge there to the best of their ability and to improve the Malaysian language to bring back all that knowledge to help develop the community. Like the whole nation.
At the same time, Dr. instructed all students to build good relationships with other students, especially to maintain the attitude and to respect all the rules of the university during the study at the university.
Students choose to study psychology at the kindergarten level, accounting, Usulutin (the basics of religion), Hokomsari (Islamic law) and counseling as they study there for two and a half years.
Please be informed that during the above meeting, HE Dr. also handed over the student acceptance certificate and passport to the students. The scholarship offers tuition, visa fees, daily meals, accommodation and airfare.
