Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Lin Jian said repeated US arms sales to Taiwan in recent months have seriously polluted the political environment for the resumption of arms control consultations. . Therefore, the Chinese side decided to cancel the talks with the United States on a new round of consultations on arms control and non-proliferation.
Lin Jian said at a briefing in Beijing that the United States is fully responsible and that China is willing to maintain relations on international arms control, but the United States must also respect China's core interests. Also create the necessary conditions for dialogue and exchange of views.
In response, State Department spokesman Matthew Miller said China had decided to follow Russia in refusing to talk to the United States to find a way to curb the nuclear arms race. But the United States will remain open to talks on ways to reduce risk with China.
