(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Mam Sok Dara, Director of the Marine Aquaculture Research and Development Center in Preah Sihanouk Province, said that his center has started hatching and raising crabs and has released more than 6 million baby crabs to serve. To supply more fishery products to the market.
This statement was made by the President of the Marine Aquaculture Research and Development Center in Sihanoukville on the occasion of a study tour and dissemination of project achievements under the theme "Local and Global Recognition for Fishery Products", which led Of Ms. M. Rachana, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Speaking during the visit, the director of the Center for Marine Aquaculture Research and Development said: "There is a lot of time left to feed, so we started to hatch and feed the baby crabs to be released into the sea, which we do no less than 5 million cubs a year."
He added that this includes the participation of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as well as other organizations such as CITEC, the Marine Inspectorate and the Fisheries Administration.
He pointed out that from the time the center distributed to farmers, JICA has been paying close attention to the distribution of fish to them, to monitor the health, all kinds of diseases or sensitivity of fish and can Make some quotes from people in the community about the differences between local fish and imported fish.
In addition, Mr. Yos Chanthana, Deputy Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Sihanoukville Province, said that the Department of Agriculture of Sihanoukville has been working closely with the Center for Marine Aquaculture Research and Development to support the center's process, including solving Challenges.
He stressed that saltwater aquaculture is important because the species of sea fish are good value and there are many for the market, especially at festivals or events, there is always a variety of fish or seafood on the table. Most people always like seafood, which is a good opportunity to develop in these areas.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture said that fish, which is a raw material or fishery product, whether fresh or saltwater, is not only natural or reared naturally, but also technically supplemented. Right, there is also the right treatment to consider the health of the consumer as the main thing, as well as give confidence to customers.
