(Kampong Thom): Mr. Ly Narun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, inaugurated 18 deep pump wells in Prasat Sambo district on July 17, 2024.
Mr. Prem Ratha, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, confirmed that for 2024, Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Rural Development has built 18 hate wells for people in 3 target districts: Santuk district, 4 Kraya communes, Kampong Svay district, Trapeang Russey commune. 02 wells and 12 temples in Prasat Sambo district, 3 wells in Chhouk commune, 3 wells in Sreung commune, 6 wells in Sambo commune, 3 wells in Chramas village and 3 wells in Koun Kaek village.
Mr. Ly Narun said that in order to contribute to the development of the water sector at the local level, people should use clean water to avoid various infectious diseases, is to provide deep wells that are not infected with germs in the community.
The use of deep wells is beneficial to all kinds of people and animals to use as needed, reducing the budget to some extent. He said that in the community, many people need clean water to use in the family to be healthy, no disease to people and animals in the community.
(Phnom Penh): In the first five months of 2024, 1330 construction projects were approved for construction with an area of 4,278 thousand square meters. Compared to the first five months of 2023, the number of construction projects decreased by 23% and the area of land decreased by 9%. This is according to the report of socio-economic trends in May 2024 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
For the first five months of 2024, construction projects were approved: 1095 housing projects (1061 Boreys and 34 condominium projects), 88 industrial constructions, 90 commercial constructions, 21 tourism constructions, 35 public constructions and Construction investment 1 project.
Oknha Nuon Rithy, CEO of KFA, said that, in fact, the construction sector seems to be declining, but we are still building, but with little growth. Construction was as low as last year, meaning that construction of residential, condominiums and apartments was declining, but construction of hotels, resorts and factories was on the rise.
He added that the construction of condominiums is currently stagnant, but industrial construction, agriculture, ports, airports are still under construction, so the construction sector is still in demand.
"In my view, the construction sector is still good and moving forward, because the construction of special economic zones can increase in large cities and along the Funan canal," he said. Cambodia earns more than 215 million USD from sales of rubber products, an increase of more than 14% in the first half of this year
