Village Chief and Deputy Chief of Khchay Village in Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province have been allowed to resume their work.
(Tbong Khmum): After being removed by the Chief of Choam Kravien Commune, Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province for almost 20 days, Mr. Keo Va, Village Chief and Mr. Thong Heng, Deputy Chief of Khchay Village, were finally allowed to continue leading the village. The original is back.
The reinstatement came after more than 100 families who loved the village chief were upset and signed a petition for intervention from the Memot district governor.
The letter of intervention was submitted to the Memot District Administration on June 28, 2024, asking the village chief to resume his work. Residents described that Mr. Keo Va is now a good village chief serving non-partisan people.
He has taken good care of the villagers from the time he became the village chief until now, he has never caused any difficulties or interruptions in serving the people. After receiving the letter from the above people, on July 15, 2024, the Governor of Memot District issued a letter to Mr. Choam Kravien commune chief on the case of changing the village chief, deputy village chief and each village member in each commune. .
On July 16, 2024, Mr. Ouch Yoeun, Chief of Choam Kravien Commune, decided to allow Mr. Keo Va to resume his position as Khchay Village Chief, and the Commune Chief issued an invitation letter to Mr. Keo Va and Mr. Thong Heng, Deputy Chiefs. Meeting to receive guidance and assign some work when joining the village chief Khchay.
