This morning, Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandith laid the foundation stone for the construction of the Samdech Preah Prohm Rattanamony Pin Sem Museum in Siem Reap.
Architecture The Khmer style architectural design project is 34 meters long, 26.6 meters wide, two floors high (ground floor and first floor), drawn by a professional officer of APSARA Authority with the approval of Samdech Preah Brahma Ratan Mony Pin Sem. The benefit of Wat Reachbo Museum is to unite the national forces to protect the national heritage between the Buddhist institutions and the empire and to attract more tourists to the resort areas of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Kingdom of Cambodia is full of rich cultural heritage through artifacts, ancient temples and inscriptions. Samdech Preah Brahma Rattanamony Pin Sem collected those items from everywhere to keep them through the people.
At present, a total of 2,575 artifacts from prehistoric times to the post-Angkorian period are collected and stored at Wat Reachbo, Siem Reap. Samdech intends to hand over the objects to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to be considered as the national cultural property.
The purpose of the construction of the Museum of Samdech Preah Brahma Ratan Mony Pin Sem to inspire students, researchers, national and international tourists to love, preserve and preserve national cultural heritage, promote beautiful traditions. Preserve artifacts made from burnt metal, metal beads, wood, bones, ivory, stone, a total of 2,575 objects dating from prehistoric times to the post-Angkorian period.
In addition, the slogan of Koh Santepheap, which is enshrined in the preamble of the Cambodian Constitution, under the slogan "Thank you for the peace and the efforts of the Royal Government" as well as contribute to the relevant ministries / institutions in the revival. Of Cambodia's tourism sector.
Please be informed that Wat Reach Bo is located on the east bank of Siem Reap River in Wat Bo Village, Sangkat Sala Kamroeuk, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. In the courtyard of the old church, there are beautiful ancient paintings of the Reamker story on the inner wall, and on each of the outer windows, there are millions of sculptures from the same lively Reamker story.
Evidence from aerial photographs shows that the pagoda site is on an old site that may have been used since ancient times. In the courtyard on the east side of the temple there is a shrine, and on the east side about 100 meters there is a large pond which looks like the general structure of a hill or temple in ancient times.
We do not have any evidence about the age of the pagoda, but according to previous research, the pagoda may have come from a tabernacle and later become a pagoda. To the east of the temple is an old gate with the same art form as the other old pagodas.
As for the construction of the temple, it is speculated that the building may have been built when Siem Reap was still under Thai rule, because on the bell there was a statue of a Siamese king. This leads to some speculation that Wat Reach Bo could have been built between the late 19th century or before 1907 AD. Separately, this pagoda also received permission to build a temple in 1921 AD, but we do not know the extent of construction yet.
Buildings repaired and preserved: * 2014 Renovation of doors, windows, statues, statues, thrones * 2019 - 2020 Renovation and preservation of the temple * 2021-2020 Renovation and preservation of the old school * 2023 Renovation of the interior of the temple .
Achievements of the pagoda: * State Buddhist Radio of Cambodia (Radio Preah Dharma) * Center for Culture and the Arts, teaching knowledge of dance, carving, painting, classical music, small skin, big skin, Pin Peat music, traditional music * Reachbo Buddhist High School Total number of students 380 - A small museum for national and international visitors to visit and learn about the culture.
