Banteay Meanchey Military sends suspect to court over motorcycle and drug theft case
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie sent a suspect to the provincial court in connection with a motorcycle theft and illegal use of drugs.
Col. Nuon Ninaro said that the victim was an employee of Crown Casino in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City. -0455 The staff working here is Chinese, with the vehicle ticket clerk guarding at night, checking all staff entering and leaving the vehicle at night.
At the time of the incident, the Chinese employee who used the above motorbike came to the motorbike and suddenly disappeared, and checked the security camera to see that the suspect was not an employee there, he stole the motorbike and rode away.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro confirmed that after receiving the complaint, the local specialized force of the Municipal Gendarmerie searched the scene and identified the suspect and arrested him at 9:00 AM on the 15th. July 2024 in front of Golden Casino in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City and brought to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for processing.
After his arrest and interrogation, the suspect confessed that he had indeed stolen the victim's motorcycle and pawned an unidentified security guard at the Goldwei Casino for 8,000 baht, spent and bought. Drugs are used up. Based on the complaint and the confession, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure, while the police are still investigating.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated. Proceedings from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
Currently, the suspect was sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Gendarmerie Criminal Bureau to follow the procedure.
