(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chiv Keng, President of the Supreme Court of Cambodia, led a delegation of Supreme Court officials, the President of the Provincial Court bordering Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos, and the President of the Court of Appeal of the jurisdiction of the border area to attend the Provincial Court Conference. The 7th Cambodia-Vietnam-Laos border, which took place on July 18-19, 2024 in Hoi An, Quang Nam Province, Vietnam.
The conference focuses on four main topics, including:
* 1: Assessment of the situation and results of the implementation of the Joint Declaration of the 6th Conference 2022 in Vientiane, Laos
* 2: Sharing experiences in the trial of criminal offenses related to illegal transnational crimes such as drug trafficking, human trafficking, forestry, natural resources and fishing offenses.
* 3: Strengthening legal mutual assistance between the courts of the three countries and
* 4: Sharing experiences on judicial reform, especially the effectiveness of the application of information technology in the judiciary.
This conference is a contribution to the promotion of law enforcement in line with the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy on the Promotion and Strengthening of the Law and the Judiciary of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Judicial conferences of the provinces bordering Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos began for the first time in 2010 in Vietnam, taking turns to host every two years. Cambodia will host the eighth conference in 2026.
