(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia, this morning, July 17, 2024, chaired a meeting of the Standing Committee of the 5th Senate with 12 agendas.
The meeting held at the Senate was attended by the permanent members of the Senate with the following agenda:
1. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Human Rights Commission for receiving complaints and investigations.
2. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Economic, Financial, Banking and Auditing Commission.
3. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Agriculture, Water Resources, Meteorology, Rural Development and Environment Investment Planning Commission.
4. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the National Defense Committee on National Assembly-Senate Relations, Inspection and Public Functions. 5. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information.
6. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Legislation and Justice Commission.
7. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religion, Culture, Fine Arts and Tourism.
8. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Committee on Health, Social Affairs, Veterans, Youth Rehabilitation, Vocational Training and Women's Affairs.
9. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Commission on Public Transport, Civil Aviation, Post, Telecommunication, Industry, Mining, Energy, Trade, Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
10. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the Commission for Investigation, Clearance and Anti-Corruption.
11. Examining and deciding on the roles, duties and responsibilities of the senators.
