The Royal Government is preparing a draft "Framework for the development and management of the river port business and the connection of the river transport system with the sea in Cambodia"
The meeting was held on July 16, 2024 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the participation of the Deputy Prime Minister, Ministers, Secretaries of State, Royal Government delegates and senior leaders of relevant ministries and institutions.
After launching the "Comprehensive Master Plan on the Cambodian Transit and Logistics System 2023-2033", the Royal Government has achieved a series of priority tasks related to the water transport sector, including the "Law on Transportation Waterway ”was recently approved and put into use.
In addition, the "Framework for the Development and Management of the River Port Business and the Connection of the River Transport System with the Sea in Cambodia" has been developed as a roadmap for relevant ministries and institutions in planning and Develop the river transport sector to be more prosperous and in line with global trends.
The framework aims to expand and increase the use of inland waterway transport systems by improving waterway transport infrastructure, improving the efficiency of port services by using modern technology and reducing logistics costs, in order to contribute to sustainability. Of Cambodia's long-term economic growth and increase regional and global competitiveness.
The meeting discussed some key points and requested the working group to review some parts of the document as well as the use of words and data to be consistent and comprehensive and highly appreciated the drafting of the "Development and Development Framework". "Managing the river port business and connecting the river transport system with the sea in Cambodia."
