Gaza: Israeli forces clashed with Islamist (Hamas) militants in several parts of the Gaza Strip on Tuesday, and Palestinian health officials say at least 30 people have been killed in clashes in the Gaza Strip. Israeli bombing of the southern and central regions. According to a release by Reuters.
The Palestinian Islamic Movement (Hamas) has accused Israel of escalating attacks in Gaza to try to thwart Arab and US mediators' efforts to reach a ceasefire.
In the southern border town of Rafah, where Israeli forces have been operating since May, five Palestinians were killed in an airstrike on a house, Gaza health officials said. A man, his wife and two children were killed near Khan Yunis, they added.
However, the Israeli military claimed that its operations in Rafah targeted militants, tunnels and Hamas military infrastructure. The airstrikes hit about 40 targets, including interceptors, military structures and buildings equipped with explosives.
The conflict erupted after Hamas launched a deadly attack on Israel on October 7. Israel has vowed to eradicate Hamas, but the nine-month war has killed more than 38,000 Palestinians.
Despite concerted efforts by Egypt and Qatar to end the conflict and release hostages, the conflict in Gaza continues to escalate.
