Thailand has experienced the closure of nearly 2,000 factories in recent years, disrupting its manufacturing sector, which accounts for nearly a quarter of its gross domestic product (GDP).
Factory closures between July 2023 and June 2024 increased by 40% compared to the previous 12 months, according to the latest unprecedented data from the Ministry of Industry. As a result, job losses increased by 80% over the same period, with more than 51,500 workers losing their jobs.
