* First: Letter of application for promotion of the relevant ministries and institutions * Second: List of civil servants applying for promotion * Third: Attach the following sub-decree of Royal Decree to promote the last rank * Fourth: Certificate of correct copy Original copy.
For sub-national administrations, please arrange the promotion according to the degree level for civil servants in accordance with the procedures in force by the end of August. In case of non-preparation within the time limit set above, the Ministry of Public Works will not accept the application and will proceed to the next year.
Artists vow not to use drugs and disseminate drug education messages at all art forums
(Phnom Penh): Artists who participated in the dissemination and training workshop on "The effects of illegal drug use" at the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts announced the dissemination of drug education messages at all art forums.
The workshop was chaired by Ms. LONG Disannara, Secretary of State and Representative of Dr. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts on 16 July 2024 under the theme "I, We, All Together for Life and Our community is drug free. ”
Neay Prek, a performer and representative of all artists, stated that, of course, drugs are a vicious catastrophe that can destroy citizens, families, society and the nation as a whole. Drugs can change people from meek to cruel, irresponsible, violent and criminal. If our young men and women indulge in drugs, the future of our family and our nation will surely be destroyed.
Neay Prek continued, "I, on behalf of all our artists, would like to solemnly announce that I will join the Royal Government and the relevant ministries, the National Anti-Drug Authority in the anti-drug campaign by promoting "Education and commit to join the Royal Government, especially the National Authority for Combating Drugs to disseminate drug education messages at all art forums."
He said that all our artists are not involved in the use of drugs to be a good example for young people and society as a whole. They cooperate with relevant ministries to help produce educational content, songs, short stories to remind young men and women to stay away from drugs, especially the knowledge gained in this time will be brought to disseminate deeply in the layer. Youth.
On that occasion, Ms. LONG DISAN NARA asked the participants in the training courses from the 25 cultural departments of the capital-province, artists, writers, producers, content producers and all stakeholders to pay attention and take this knowledge. Expand, disseminate and continue to reach out to the base of our work for the safety of our society as a whole.
