Kandal Provincial Governor Orders Authorities and Officials to crack down on illegal fishing gear, especially those who post on social media
(Kandal): The Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, ordered the relevant authorities to cooperate with professional officers to crack down on the production of illegal fishing gear at the local level, especially those who post for sale on social media, which leads to the destruction of natural resources and fish. As well as dangerous to humans.
A man has been arrested for stealing a fishing tackle on social media. The arrest was made on July 15, 2024 by the Kandal Provincial Fisheries Administration in cooperation with local authorities under the coordination of the Kandal Provincial Deputy Prosecutor, who visited the location in Traing Leu village, Ta Ek commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province. .
Heng Sophearith, director of the Kandal Fisheries Administration, confirmed that the operation, which led to the arrest of one of the suspects, a manufacturer and distributor of illegal fishing gear, took place on the orders of Kouch Chamroeun. Posting on social media, Tek Tek posted the sale of these illegal devices to the public, while in this case, the suspect admitted that he had actually stolen the product and distributed it in some provinces.
Mr. Heng Sophearith said that after the arrest and confiscation of the suspects, the case was sent to court to be processed according to the law, as this case is a fishing offense that can not be tolerated due to the people. This suspect has been stealing this illegal device for a long time.
At the same time, Mr. Heng Sophearith also called on all citizens to cooperate with the authorities or the Fisheries Administration to eliminate illegal fishing in your villages and communities. Fishing or stealing illegal fishing gear will take immediate action without exception.
