Government signs $ 140 million new loan agreement in first quarter, down more than 70%
(Phnom Penh): In the first quarter of 2024, the Royal Government of Cambodia signed a new loan agreement with development partners amounting to about 140 million US dollars, a decrease of about 71% compared to the same period in 2023 as of the first quarter This year, Cambodia has more than $ 11.09 billion in debt, which is at risk and manageable.
The Ministry of Economy stated, "These loans are all high-concessional loans, with an average of 40% of donations." "The purpose of these new loan agreements is to meet the financing needs of the Royal Government's priority areas to contribute to sustaining long-term growth and increasing economic productivity or productivity."
In the first quarter of 2024, the new government will withdraw 141.64 million US dollars in concessional loans, a decrease of 47%. 88% of this cash withdrawal will be used for infrastructure and 12% for other priority sectors.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News that the reduction in credit agreements could be due to the Royal Government having a reserve budget in response to its public development projects. On the other hand, the government may not want to increase public debt compared to the needs of public investment projects.
Cambodia's debt situation is still assessed as manageable, remaining "sustainable" and "low risk" despite the impact of the Cambodian economy on the spread of Kovid 19 and other factors. From the outside.
Ministry of Education Introduces New Reading Enhancement Program Using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to Improve Reading Ability for Students Nationwide
(Phnom Penh): The Center for Digital Education and Distance Education of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, under the leadership of Dr. San Vathana, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and colleagues, has developed the first mobile technology education application that uses artificial intelligence to Support the ability to read in Khmer, especially for high school students with reading problems by being named "literate".
* Difficulty level of the text: Level reading text from the Khmer textbook for reading practice
* Word recognition and word meaning: Difficult words in each text have an explanation of the meaning
* Hearing: Each text contains sample reading sounds using artificially generated sounds.
* Quiz Practice: Students can practice quizzes organized by an international reading proficiency test system.
* Essay writing practice: Students can send handwritten essays and send them to the teacher for direct feedback.
* Practice reading: Students can also practice reading and send the voice to the teacher for improvement and evaluation.
* Accurate reading and speed: Students can measure reading accuracy and speed of reading with artificial intelligence technology to evaluate the score.
