At the same time, according to Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, in the first five months of 2024, Cambodia imported a total of 16,204 vehicles with taxes and duties. 989.895 million riels, equivalent to more than 240 million dollars.
Mr. Soeun Dara stated, "If we look at the trend of car imports from abroad in recent years, the volume of car imports to Cambodia tends to decrease every year as the country's economic growth has changed. "The mindset of the people as well as the consumers to buy a new car instead of a used car."
In addition, Mr. Soeun Dara pointed out that the decrease was due to the new cars receiving both quality assurance and maintenance services, with buyers not worrying about repairs or high maintenance costs, with an average five-year warranty. Used cars can have problems during the purchase as well.
According to the Executive Director of the Cambodian Automobile Industry, this factor has led to a steady increase in demand for new cars from 10% of the market share in 2013 to about 45% in 2023.
At the same time, Mr. Soeun Dara said that as the growth of car assembly plants increased, car imports from abroad continued to decline. This factor has provided many benefits to Cambodia, including:
* Reduce trade deficit * Increase and attract investment in heavy industry to Cambodia * Create jobs, transfer technology and technical skills * Promote national economic growth due to reduced customs revenue but will increase tax revenue instead Cars are cheaper than imports.
It should be noted that in the first quarter of 2024, sales of both new and used cars in Cambodia decreased by about 25%, of which sales of used cars decreased by almost 30% while sales of new cars decreased. About 20%.
