(Phnom Penh): His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Tuesday morning, July 16, 2024, visited and inaugurated the achievements of his remaining office building. Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC)
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet's opportunity to visit and inaugurate the achievements of the remaining ECCC Performance Building:
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that he was very pleased to attend and deliver a speech at the "Visit and Inauguration of Achievements at the ECCC Remaining Function Building." Organized by the Office of the Council of Ministers and the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Khmer Rouge regime had left unimaginable damage and unforgettable suffering to the Cambodian people to this day.
* President Hun Manet stated that even though decades have passed, the Cambodian people continue to fight against those pains. Survivors struggle to cope with the emotional and physical crisis of losing family members and personal health on a regular basis.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that Samdech would like to take this rare opportunity to express his deepest gratitude and always remember the great and priceless work and merits of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen. Liberated the nation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and brought peace, national unity, national unity and territorial integrity in its 500-year history through the introduction of win-win politics.
* Prime Minister Hun Manet stated that win-win politics is the foundation of lasting peace, as this win-win policy eliminates racial, religious and sectarian discrimination and empowers Cambodians. All live in harmony in society together.
* President Hun Manet stated that through this win-win policy, the Royal Government of Cambodia also established the ECCC. With the excellent cooperation of the United Nations and the financial support of the international community to provide justice to the victims of the Khmer Rouge regime, to reconcile the divided society, to eradicate the culture of impunity and to send a message to the main Leaders of countries around the world about the consequences of their atrocities.
* President Hun Manet claims that humanity does not need war
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet advised to keep the relevant documents of the ECCC properly
* Prince Hun Manet stated that the policy of killing people is unacceptable that the next generation of Cambodians must remember
Samdech Hun Sen encourages both foreigners and Cambodians who want to study original documents related to the genocidal regime
* Prince Hun Manet recommends increasing the digital storage of documents to prevent loss as these documents cannot be returned for another 16 years
* President Hun Manet, the history of Cambodia, must not be left alone, that is, open up opportunities for foreigners to research, especially the courts with historical character
