(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 15, 2024, Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, met for the second time with the five health professional committees, including doctors, dentists, midwives, nurses and pharmacists. .
The event was held at the Ministry of Health and through the ZOOM system with the participation of 907 leaders and health advisers, leaders and officials of the five health professional committees.
The purpose of this meeting was to 1) review the key points discussed at the first meeting and 2) to review the current work to improve the management of health professionals, especially the implementation of professional ethics. Health.
The Minister welcomed and encouraged all health professional committees to continue to strengthen cooperation, focusing on compliance with the work and compliance with the laws and regulations in force, training and conduct ethical practice. On accuracy, both technical and soft skills.
In particular, increasing training, education, dissemination, maximum prevention of professional phenomena, respect for client rights and general administration work as a model to ensure that the right service, quality and safety in accordance with pedagogy and ethics, while maintaining the interests of patients and Customer priority is something that everyone, on behalf of the five health professionals, must continue to strive for anytime, anywhere.
The Minister also clarified the joint role of the Health Professions Committee and the core duties of each professional committee. In addition, the Minister encouraged all health professional committees to prepare a comprehensive implementation plan and to monitor and evaluate regularly to achieve their work priorities.
In response, the five health professional committees expressed their satisfaction and emphasized the importance of this event, especially the good advice of the Minister, which is useful for further improvement and development of their work.
The Minister expressed his appreciation for the past work of the Health Professions Committee and its commitment to continue its noble mission. He also reaffirmed the Ministry's support for the implementation of the work of the Health Professions Committee and hoped for positive results in better service to the people.
