Prahok flour is a project of Confirel under the discovery of Oknha Dr. Hay Ly Eang, whose project started in early 2023. The Prahok Flour Project aims to innovate and promote traditional Khmer prahok by turning it into a powder form that is easy to use and high quality. Prahok is an important ingredient in Khmer cuisine because of its indispensable flavor and importance for Khmer culture.
"By converting prahok into flour, we not only preserve this traditional delicacy, but also make it easier to use, hygienic and usable," he said. Khmer and some foreign food as well, so prairie flour is most suitable for local and international markets.
At the same time, the colleagues of Dr. Mrs. Mao Rachana, Project Manager of Confirel also said, "The purpose of the project is to share the Khmer cultural heritage and unique taste of our Khmer prahok with those who like to find new food. Different from around the world and to sell in the local market and export prahok flour to international markets successfully and can ensure that the standard, safety and quality of food.
But from there, she said, the goal is to focus on the entire production process, from sourcing raw materials to packaging and distribution, with a strong emphasis on sustainability and community development, and the need for prahok flour. Made from fish-processed prahok on the Tonle Sap Lake, the largest lake in Southeast Asia and located in Cambodia, where it is the most important ecosystem, the largest fish and wildlife sanctuary.
"As this is a fishery product, we have a lot of demand for entry into the international market, for example, information related to the supply of raw materials or production inputs and export procedures," he said.
Third, the creation and implementation of a digital tracking system. Through this system, customers can scan the QR code affixed on the product to observe the digital trace of the entire process of modern Khmer prahok powder products from farms or fishing boats to the food table. This not only demonstrates the company's commitment to improving quality and risk management, but also builds trust with customers and stakeholders.
