The primary is that of a larger size. In the first half of this year, China's exports and imports exceeded 21 trillion yuan for the first time compared to the same period in history, breaking a record high again. Exports and imports in the second quarter rose 7.4 percent from the same period in 2023, indicating that the trend towards improving China's foreign trade has been further strengthened.
From a global perspective, the current geopolitical situation is increasingly tense and trade protectionism is recovering, posing a challenge to global trade. Why can China's foreign trade increase against the trend? Wang Jun, a Chinese economist, analyzed that this first benefited from the capital excellence of Chinese production and the superiority of China's complete production and supply chain.
In addition, global demand for Chinese products is currently strong, boosting Chinese exports. In addition, the transformation and improvement of the Chinese economy has undergone continuous breakthroughs, especially the rapid growth in the production of new quality products. These factors have led to the gradual improvement of trade. With Chinese foreigners.
Many international financial institutions, such as the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund, have recently raised their expectations for China's 2024 economic growth. This reaffirms that the Chinese economy remains the largest engine of global growth, and that the Chinese market is a market that foreign investors cannot abandon.
Faced with a complex and volatile international environment, China's economy is strong and resilient to overcoming difficulties and advancing to share high-quality dividends and development opportunities with the world.
