(Shanghai) - The Chinese government has provided support to Cambodia in human resource development through scholarship programs and study tours, said Secretary-General of the Ministry of Economy and Finance Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State In all fields, which has provided opportunities for many Cambodian students, professors and civil servants to study, understand and gain experience every year in multidisciplinary and multidisciplinary areas in China.
He made the remarks at the opening ceremony of a training seminar on "Achievement Budget: China's Experience" at the Asia-Pacific Institute for Finance and Development (AFDI) in Shanghai on July 15, 2024.
The Institute of Economics and Finance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in collaboration with the Asia-Pacific Institute of Finance and Development (AFDI) of Shanghai, on July 15, 2024, held a training workshop on "Achievement Budget: China Experience". Women leaders of relevant ministries and institutions and 30 trainers from the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The workshop was organized by the Institute of Economics and Finance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in collaboration with the AFDI Institute, with 30 female participants, leaders of relevant ministries and institutions, and 30 trainers from the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The opening ceremony was attended by Prof. Dr. LU Wenbin, President of the National Institute of Accounting and the Asia-Pacific Institute for Finance and Development (SNAI & AFDI), Shanghai, with the participation of female participants, leaders, Secretary of State, Under Secretary of State. Relevant institutions, professors, lecturers and speakers, as well as relevant professional officials from both Cambodia and China.
Speaking on the occasion, the head of the delegation said that Cambodia and China have a long tradition of friendship and solidarity. This relationship of friendship and solidarity has been enhanced to the level of strategic cooperation in all aspects.
Since 2017, Cambodia and China have gone through decades of enhancing comprehensive strategic partnership and bilateral cooperation in all fields, including politics, economy, society and culture, in order to further promote the socio-economic development of the two countries. Advancement in the context of the Industrial Revolution and the rapid growth of information and digital technologies.
This workshop is a special curriculum in 2024 for the target female trainees, who are the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the relevant ministries and institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia, who are starting to pilot the implementation of the budget, information, achievements, so that the participants can understand and Citing good experiences from international excellence and practical experience in reforming China's budget management system.
The overall goal of Cambodia's public financial management reform program is to transform the Cambodian budget system into a result-oriented or achievement-decentralized budget system in line with international standards and excellence to contribute to national socio-economic development.
