Informal Economy Group Condemns Extremist Groups for Exaggerating Information Attacking Government Involving Transport Operators
(Phnom Penh): The Informal Economic Group of the Committee of Civil Society Organizations on July 15, 2024 issued a statement condemning the extremists who took the opportunity to fabricate exaggerated information to attack the Royal Government of Cambodia for political gain. Involved in the transport sector.
"We are all entrepreneurs in the informal economy of civil society organizations, most of whom are in the transport sector (PassApp), motodup, business owners, vendors, traders, etc. Please express our condolences to the extremists. "Who always fabricate false information to confuse the people in terms of their political exploitation to attack the government."
Recently, a fake story was posted on VOD's Facebook page, alleging that "Prime Minister Hun Manet paved the way for the business of electric vehicles after last year's refusal to allow Vietnamese companies to transport tourists to the economic zone. "In Cambodia, using 2,500 cars powered by electricity."
The Prime Minister also revealed that he had received information that a group of people were mobilizing motodup and tricycle riders to protest against the government, on the pretext that the government allowed foreign companies to invest in taxis. In Cambodia. At the same time, the President also warned against fabricating information in this negative sense that will face the law without exception.
The Informal Economy Group of the Civil Society Coalition Committee has expressed regret over a handful of extremists who continue to pollute society, misrepresent information for political gain as the country develops, and the government is working to make the country a better place. The nation is growing, competing on an equal footing with countries in the region and the world.
The Code of Informal Economy calls on the Cambodian people to unite and cultivate a stronger sense of patriotism, especially to call on the competent authorities to take legal action against those who fabricate and create false information in the form of profiteering. Politics that wants to cause chaos in Cambodia.
