Ministry of Agriculture organizes a visit to promote achievements under the theme: "Local and Global Recognition for Fishery Products"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and UNIDO have organized a visit to journalists, experts and stakeholders to study and disseminate the achievements of one of their projects under the theme: "Local and Global Recognition for Fishery products.
The visit will last for four days, from July 15 to 18, 2024, with more than 40 journalists from 21 institutions who will travel to three capitals and provinces, including Phnom Penh, Koh Kong and Sihanoukville. And so on.
The study tour was led and coordinated by Ms. M. Rachana, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with the participation of leaders and experts of the Fisheries Administration (FIA), Representative of the European Union to Cambodia, UNIDO and journalists.
The purpose of this visit is to promote the project achievements and promote safe and high quality fishery products in the domestic market and to the international market under the post-harvest fisheries development project CAPFISH-Capture, funded by the EU to accelerate quality recognition. And Cambodia's food safety from national to international.
The Sustainable and Environmental Fisheries Promotion Program (CAPFish) is a EU-funded fisheries program aimed at contributing to the Royal Government of Cambodia's long-term vision for social and economic development, food security and cutting. Reduce poverty.
