Drug addict who killed an elderly woman in Battambang City and fled to hide in the forest for several days, has now been arrested by the authorities
(Battambang): A suspected drug user who rode a bicycle to kill an 85-year-old woman on the street and fled into the forest for several days, causing people to panic, was intercepted by hundreds of police forces. Yes, at 17:30 on July 14, 2024 at a forest point in O'Pong Moan village, Ta Kream commune, Banan district, Battambang province.
Mr. Chhoeung Kimsong, Deputy Commissioner of Battambang Provincial Police in charge of Minor Crimes, said that the suspect was abducted by the police as he was walking out of the forest to cross the road to the village. He was starving for days in the forest.
He said that hundreds of police forces, including provincial commissioners, district inspectors, border towns, military forces, local authorities, people and people, using professional measures for 8 nights and 9 days to search and hide and intercept. The suspect did.
Mr. Chhoeung Kimsong added that the arrested suspect had the skills to walk in the forest so that he could stay in the forest for a long time because according to the villagers, he used to walk in the forest with his mother for more than 10 years when he was young. And due to the complex geography, it is difficult for the authorities to find out.
According to the Battambang Provincial Police, the suspect was Soeun Tun, a 25-year-old man currently living in O'Pong Moan village, Ta Kream commune, Banan district, Battambang province. He was taken to a drug rehabilitation center at the center when the police caught him and had a bad temper.
The source added that on July 6, 2024, at 13:10, at Group 6, Chrap Krasaing Village, Wat Kor Sangkat, Battambang City, Battambang Province, the suspect was riding a bicycle armed with a knife. Hor Pok, an 84-year-old female resident of the scene, died at the scene, and the suspect fled on a bicycle.
After the killing, the suspect fled into the village, causing fear among the villagers for fear that the villain would continue to kill people, but he was eventually arrested and sent to the provincial commissioner for legal action. Legal way.
