Mr. Oknha Kuy Leang Ky and Mrs. Khuon Khundy donated 39 pagodas in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): Mrs. Khuon Khundy, Senator and Chairman of Kampong Svay District Field Team and Mr. Kuy Leang Ky on July 14, 2024, presented candles and relics to 39 monks in Kampong Svay district. Kampong Thom Province. The ceremony was attended by Mrs. Lum Kuntheary, Deputy Governor, Major General Men Ly, Provincial Police Commissioner, leaders, government officials, district authorities and many people.
Ms. Khuon Khundy said that this ceremony can take place because the country is completely peaceful, has developed in all fields, including the field of Buddhism has grown significantly. The offering of Preah Vossa candles, as well as food and suffixes, to be given to the monks now so that the monks can burn them, light them, offer sacrifices to God, and study the Dharma of the Dharma of our Master Samma Samput.
She said that at present, the field of Buddhism is growing rapidly, no matter where people live, there are pagodas, temples, and hermitages for those who respect and preserve Buddhism in the traditional Khmer way under the leadership of Samdech Bovathibati. Hun Manet supports the people to preserve the traditions of our ancestors better.
She stated that in the pagodas throughout Cambodia, there is the construction of temples, pavilions, halls for the shrine and for the monks to live. If the nation is not at peace, there is no progress, the people will not have a decent standard of living, and the construction of pagodas will not happen, and Buddhists will not come to the festivals at the pagodas.
She called on all Buddhists who believe in Buddhism to continue to participate in almsgiving, help build pagodas, schools and especially build good deeds for everyone to make the society a society. There is no social violence, only a culture of mutual tolerance.
On that occasion, Mrs. Khuon Khundy, Mr. Oknha Kuy Leang Ky and friends and relatives also held a ceremony to give candles to Preah Vossa in accordance with our Buddhist tradition to dedicate merits to ancestors, relatives, blood, cadres, warriors and warriors. Sacrifice death in the cause of the motherland, which passed away to the next world as well.
It should be noted that in each pagoda received a pair of candles, orange juice, noodles, pure water, fish sauce, soy sauce, some materials and some money.
Mr. Sok Lou and his wife and relatives donated candles to commemorate Preah Vossa and gifts to the monks at Wat Por Rainsy Vattanaream (called Wat Sangke Vear) in Bavel district.
