Inauguration Ceremony of the Assembly Hall and Other Achievements in Wat Mongkul, Ta Ream Province, Preah Sre District, Mongkul Borey District
(Banteay Meanchey): On July 14, 2024, in Mongkul pagoda, Ta Ream province, Preah Sre, in Talom commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, the inauguration ceremony of the synagogue and other achievements in the pagoda were officially inaugurated.
The ceremony was attended by His Excellency Sil Nhean Thul Sothea, Honorary King of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Chhoeun Krayong, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mr. Rath Dasinang, Governor of Mongkul Borei District, Mr. Beav Than, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Cult and Religion More than 1,000 students, members of the Armed Forces, Police, Citizens and Ta Chi Yai Chi
Mr. Beav Than said that according to the report of the Chief Inspector of Wat Preah Sre, it was written that this pagoda was built in 1811, equal to 213 years ago, and this pagoda has a total area of 33,402.5 square meters during the Pol Pot era. This pagoda was destroyed after the day of liberation in 1979 under the leadership of the Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation, led by the Cambodian People's Party, Buddhism was revived.
Mr. Beav Than continued that under the leadership of many chief priests, Wat Preah Sre has built achievements in many pagodas, including the construction of a new synagogue with a size of 25 meters by 43 meters at a total cost of $ 850,000 inaugurated today.
He said that pagodas across the country during the 1979 Pol Pot floods were decapitated by the Khmer Rouge, and temples and halls were used as fertilizer by the Khmer Rouge after the liberation on January 7, 1979. Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, pagodas across the country were revived, including the monks of Vihear and Sala Chan.
Mr. Chhoeun Krayong continued that in 2024, through the decision to give the election to Samdech President Hun Manet as the Prime Minister of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, Samdech took the sub-national level to pay attention to building the empire and Buddhism to go hand in hand, if there is progress, but the realm of Buddhism is degenerating, then it is impossible for the two to go hand in hand.
Mr. Chhoeun Krayong continued that this Preah Sre pagoda, with the attention of the Banteay Meanchey provincial authorities, the Banteay Meanchey cult, the committee of pagoda abbots, local expatriates, local people and Buddhists have worked together to build a synagogue and other achievements. In Wat Mongkul, Khet Ream, Preah Sre in Mongkul Borei district, this pagoda is constantly growing.
He also instructed and reminded all monks, abbots, pagoda committees to know how to maintain all the existing achievements well and to participate and develop Wat Preah Sre to be more prosperous in order to turn the pagoda into a place. Nursery training the next generation to become the human resources that the nation needs.
Mr. Chhoeun Krayong presented about 50 certificates of appreciation to those who have worked hard to build this pagoda, in which philanthropists have donated papaya noodles and solidarity rice to those who have enjoyed a happy meal. Mr. Chea Sophara Taken the Chairman of Tbong Khmum Provincial Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Pen Kosal, replacing Dr. Cheam Chansophoan
