A helicopter that lost contact with air force headquarters in the Cardamom Mountains, Pursat and Koh Kong provinces on July 12, 2024, is still under search and rescue, the statement said.
The Defense Ministry said the accident happened during a training flight, which was part of the Air Force's regular training flight plan in the area. The helicopter consists of two people: a captain and a pilot.
The Ministry of National Defense would like to thank the efforts of the forces and the Provincial Unity Command, which have joined the search with the unit and the expert team. Thank you to the private sector for their willingness to join the search and rescue team.
According to the Ministry of National Defense, due to the weather conditions at the operation site, it is very foggy and the rescue team has already set the direction to deploy forces in this area. Therefore, the private sector should allow the search and rescue team to continue operating first.
