Please be informed that the rainy season lasts for 3 months to contribute to the support of the monks who are still in the pagoda to learn various disciplines during the 3 months of this rainy season. Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to study the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings.
For each pagoda during the three months of the rainy season, it is not allowed to travel far and wide during the day and night, except for important tasks such as parents who are seriously ill or going to perform dharma, etc., determined to return. Within 7 days.
Believers in Buddhism often celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible, and offering votive candles, food and suffixes. Monks now, for monks to burn, worship and study the Dharma of the Dharma, our Samma Samput, our teacher.
General Sao Sokha: For 31 years, the Royal Gendarmerie has been involved in preventing any attempt to provoke unrest in order to maintain peace in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, highlighted some of the key qualities of the Royal Gendarmerie over the past 31 years by continuing to promote the spirit of prevention. All attempts to cause unrest in all forms to protect peace, security and order in Cambodian society.
General Sao Sokha demonstrated these qualities at the commemoration of the 31st anniversary of the establishment of the National Gendarmerie (July 14, 1993 - July 14, 2020), taking place this morning, July 14, 2024. Presided over by General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense at the Kambol Military Police Institute.
At the same time, General Sao Sokha emphasized that the National Gendarmerie is committed to supporting and implementing with a high sense of responsibility and political program of the Royal Government of the 7th mandate, especially fully supporting the Prek Chik Funan Techo project. The construction site will open on August 5, 2024.
General Sao Sokha added that the National Gendarmerie has been active in the area as assigned to support the implementation of the Royal Government's political program to help the people and support the local authorities.
General Sao Sokha claimed that the Royal Gendarmerie has sharpened its strategic plan for reform in accordance with four principles: first: mobilization, second: order, third: modernization and fourth: efficiency. In that, modernization of education, training and training has been used as a basis for reform.
Please be reminded that the Royal Gendarmerie was first established in 1957 under the name "Khmer Royal Gendarmerie". In 1971, the Khmer Royal Gendarmerie was renamed the "National Gendarmerie". During the Khmer Rouge regime, the military police institution was abolished. Until July 14, 1993, the Royal Gendarmerie was re-established.
