(Banteay Meanchey): The local police force of Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, sent 3 Thai suspects to the provincial court to follow the relevant procedures in 4 cases.
The arrest of the three suspects involved 4 cases: 1: aggravated intentional violence, 2: aggravated theft, 3: possession or transportation of weapons without permission, 4: storage, trafficking and use by Illegal drugs committed at 07:00 on July 11, 2024 at the point of a 12-story building with chalk in Samaki Meanchey village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city.
After being arrested and interrogated, the three suspects confessed that they were involved in the above allegations. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has built a case and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lt. Col. Men Phirum, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of crime investigation and crackdown, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and coordinated. Proceedings from Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
