(Phnom Penh): The Star Festival 2024 started from 12 to 14 July 2024, highlighting the traditional culture of Japan and Cambodia together to make the two countries closer through the people and people. People get to know each other's culture and enjoy new experiences, learn about Japanese culture and become closer to Japan.
On that occasion, the Japanese Ambassador said that the Star Festival or Tanabata Festival 2024 is a traditional Japanese festival that is always held on July 7 every year. On Tanabata Day, Japanese people write their wishes on colored paper and hang them on bamboo branches with various Tanabata ornaments.
He added that in Cambodia, this year's Star Festival, organized by the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center (CJCC), the Japan Foundation, the Phnom Penh Liaison Office and the Embassy of Japan, will run from today until July 14. The purpose of this festival is to show the traditional culture of Tanabata festival to the people of Cambodia and to build and promote good relations between Japan and Cambodia.
