Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources opens the gates of Stung Sreng I and Stung Sreng II reservoirs to irrigate more than 2,000 hectares of rain-fed rice in Kralanh district, Siem Reap province.
(Oddar Meanchey): The Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Oddar Meanchey Province on July 13, 2024 opened the gates of Stung Sreng I Reservoir and Teuk Stung Sreng II Reservoir in Chong Kal District to send water through the river. Sreng to the district to store and distribute through the construction of Stung Kralanh dam to irrigate 2,300 hectares of rain-fed rice in Ta An commune, Kampong Thkov, Sambour and Kralanh commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province.
With the opening of the Stung Sreng I and Stung Sreng II reservoirs, Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, also made a request to farmers who are cultivating rain-fed rice as well as other mixed crops. In some villages and communes in Kralanh district, Siem Reap province, please pay attention to the use of water received from Oddar Meanchey province, use it for the purpose and use it sparingly.
According to Mr. Nhen Kuon, the potential reservoirs in Oddar Meanchey province are Stung Sreng 1 Reservoir and Stung Sreng 2 Reservoir located in Chong Kal District, with water source from Dam 05, Ta Mok Dam. New and its submerged surface.
He added that the Stung Sreng 1 district basin was built and developed in 2010 and completed in 2015 with a storage capacity of 153 million cubic meters. Separately, Stung Sreng 2 Reservoir was built and developed in 2013 and completed in 2019 with a storage capacity of 258 million cubic meters and also has the role of supplying additional water to Stung Sreng 1 Reservoir.
