Michel Trané said that on the left and right doorstep of the temple, there are inscriptions describing historical events as ancient cultural currents. The significance of these two inscriptions is to confirm the connection between the Chenla dynasty and the Phnom dynasty, that is, between Suryavong and Somvong. Because these two dynasties are all descendants from all the Cambodian tribes.
In addition to the issue of the dynasty of the Khmer kings who ruled in ancient times, we also learned about the historical politics of the kingdom of Chenla, liberating the people of Chenla from the Sui Sa Akhar chain, that is, liberating themselves from the control of the mountain kingdom.
It should be informed that Baksey Chamkrong temple is located in the middle of dense forest on the left side of the road and about 150 meters north of Phnom Bakheng, with a staircase built of limestone and red brick. Around this temple, there are also some small temples built of brick, some of which are obscured by plants. Baksey Chamkrong temple has five levels of cones, including the floor under the brick temple facing east.
