(Kandal): Brigadier General Sam Tola, Commander of Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, organized a blood donation program with the participation of many forces under his command, including some Cambodians from abroad, at the headquarters today. July 11, 2024.
Brigadier General Commander said that in addition to the work of Snuol, the Kandal Provincial Police also participated in various social and humanitarian activities. This is the 13th time since 2015 that the Provincial Gendarmerie has donated blood to save lives.
"To celebrate the 31st anniversary of the establishment of the Gendarmerie, we have created this campaign with many deputy officers, including the participation of the people, resulting in a total of 110 blocks of blood." . He added.
So far, 75 of our Deputy Chiefs of the Armed Forces have received medals and certificates of appreciation from the National Blood Transfusion Center for donating blood five or more times, up to 10 times, and recently 11 other forces. Also received a medal.
At the same time, Colonel Pok Sang, Deputy Commander of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie, claimed that donating blood did not harm his health, but only made him physically and mentally healthy. Has donated blood many times and asked to donate blood to save lives.
On this occasion, Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, called for blood donation, while 6 minutes need 1 block of blood to save lives, and it is necessary to need 160,000 blocks of blood per year to meet this blood demand. Donating blood does not affect health, and the only source of blood is from people who do not have a pharmaceutical factory, and do not wait until it is too late to donate blood.
He would also like to express his deep gratitude to the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie for always donating blood and inspiring this movement to the soldiers and officers, as well as the people to donate blood vigorously, in fact, today received 110 bags of blood. .
