Stay tuned for the full talk at 6pm, which will air on Fresh News TV and other channels. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor: Cambodian Veterans Day is held to commemorate the heroism and honor the merits and merits of veterans to the nation and the people
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Honorary Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Cham Province, said that the Cambodian Veterans Day is held to commemorate the heroism and honor and merits of the veterans to the nation and Cambodian people.
This was stated by the Provincial Governor on the morning of July 13, 2024 on the occasion of the 17th anniversary of the Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2024 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall, with the participation of Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of the Provincial Council and former members. More than 400 Cambodian fighters, relevant units.
The provincial governor stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia issued Resolution 31 Pillar dated June 20, 2007, designating June 21 as the Day of Cambodian Veterans, and organizing the Day of Cambodian Veterans Day to commemorate the heroism. And to honor the merits of veterans to the nation and the people of Cambodia.
In addition to commemorating the heroism and merits of veterans, this day also aims to spread awareness about veterans, inspire the movement to support veterans, promote the role of veterans in society and promote patriotic spirit at all levels. The people, the armed forces, especially the youth, to turn the youth into worthy pillars and successors with strong ideals, strong and dignified.
Currently, the Cambodian Veterans Association has Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, and Samdech President Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as the First Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
Both Samdechs have always regarded the spirit of courageous struggle and sincere sacrifice of the Cambodian warriors, the great merits recorded in the national history and sacrificed everything for the cause of the motherland, which is a great example of patriotic heroism. Of all veterans.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the committee of Kampong Cham Veterans Association has made efforts to improve the living standards of veterans by inspecting the actual living conditions at the local level and found some veterans have land. Some are homeless, some have unsuitable houses, some have no land, some have no houses and some live on public land.
Based on this finding, the Kampong Cham Provincial Association has requested for the construction of houses, the provision of social land concessions and the proper renovation of houses until now, which are the precious gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Thipadei Hun. Manet also received support from the administration of Kampong Cham and provincial leaders to the local level and philanthropists.
