Ministry of Public Works Calls for Increased Caution on Navigation at Chak Angre Krom-Prek Pra Bridge Construction Site
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has issued a notice to all operators and water transport companies to pay attention to driving the ship with extreme caution when crossing the bridge project across the Bassac River (Chak Angre). Krom - Prek Pra), located west of Chak Angre Krom, Khan Meanchey and east of Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
In a statement from the Ministry of Public Works received by Fresh News on the evening of July 12, 2024, it was stated that the construction of the bridge across the Bassac River has officially started and is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2027. During this time, the construction site of the bridge, the bridge, the narrow waterway, which may interfere with navigation.
To ensure the safety of navigators traveling along the Bassac River through the construction site of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, please call on the public, people, operators and all water transport companies to pay attention to driving with Be very careful and follow the instructions below:
1: Slow down the ship and drive in a safe space with signs and airbags.
2. Maintain a safe driving distance, especially during the rainy season with strong currents and whirlwinds to avoid the risk of collisions when crossing narrow alleys or near construction sites.
3. Give priority to the ships of the construction site and follow the signs and instructions from the bridge construction staff.
4: Within 500 meters from the construction site, anchors are not allowed to stop or stay.
5. Ships passing through the construction site must travel to the designated location.
6. It is forbidden to overtake and speed, causing strong waves and to maintain a safety distance of 500 meters. Oddar Meanchey Provincial Armed Forces arrested 4 suspects and confiscated some drugs in Anlong Veng district.
