The following is the announcement of the Real Estate and Mortgage Business Regulator: Cambodian Red Cross, Battambang Province, opened a training course on volunteer work and first aid for advisors and youth at Hun Sen Treng High School.
(Battambang): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Battambang Province on July 10, 2024, with Mr. Sok Lou as the Chairman of the Branch Committee, opened a training course for Cambodian Red Cross volunteer work and first aid to the Cambodian Red Cross Advisors and Youth. 60 participants at Hun Sen Treng High School, Rattanak Mondul District, with the participation of the High School Principal, Youth Advisor and CRC Youth, a total of 70 participants at Hun Sen Treng High School.
The purpose of this training is to increase the knowledge capacity, including the history of the Red Cross movement, the Red Crescent, health and skills to save the lives of victims and reduce deaths by accident.
On that occasion, Mr. Yan Odom, Deputy Director of Peam Branch, sent a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of the Branch Committee with love and remembrance to the teachers and advisors. All young people and students who have dedicated their time to participating in the Cambodian Red Cross humanitarian movement aim to share the suffering of the victims and the vulnerable in other ways.
The Deputy Director of the Branch stated that the purpose of opening this course is to strengthen and expand the humanitarian force, in which our Red Cross youth have a deeper understanding of the Red Cross movement, its role, duties and first aid, which is a subject that can help. Reduce the pain of victims of various accidents before the ambulance or medical team arrives.
1: History of the Red Cross, Red Crescent and Cambodian Red Cross Foundation Principles 2: CRC Youth Management and the Establishment of a Sustainable Youth Club 3: Disaster Management and Climate Change 4: Road Safety and Health 5 : Work to improve the environment in 6 educational institutions: First aid.
Mr. Yan Udom, Deputy Director of the branch, said that although this course is only one day short, but it provides a lot of knowledge and basic to the youth of the Cambodian Red Cross in order to enhance the spirit of young people to be able to participate. With the Red Cross movement, the Red Crescent reduces the suffering of all affected people and to enhance the reputation of the Cambodian Red Cross, the only humanitarian association in Cambodia.
