CNN to cut 100 jobs to focus on digital
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - CNN will cut about 100 jobs as part of its plans to consolidate its information operations and boost its digital business, according to an internal memorandum obtained by Reuters on Thursday.
Senior Minister Kitech Continues to Meet Nearly 400 More Victims in Leng Channa Case, Seventh Meeting
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 12, 2024, Mr. Kitech, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chief of the Royal Government Lawyer, continued to meet with more than 400 victims in the company case of former tycoon Leng Channa. Group 7 The meeting was held at the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ky Tech claimed that after receiving the authority from Samdech Hun Manet, the Royal Government's lawyers immediately set up an emergency working group to provide means to the victims. Mr. Ky Tech emphasized that the next step, he will lead the Royal Government's lawyers to the provinces to provide convenience to people to reduce the cost of travel to Phnom Penh.
As for the victims who are working abroad, Mr. Ky Tech claims that they can contact the Cambodian Embassy in the country to get a thumbprint without having to travel to Cambodia. .
He confirmed that the seventh meeting with nearly 400 people now after the government lawyers have already met with the victims. He said that according to the information he received, there were more than 3,000 people who claimed to be victims in this case.
According to lawyer Ky Tech, the current meeting with the victims is not different from the previous ones, which are held for two main purposes, including the first: the delegation of legal representation to the lawyer through Voluntary fingerprinting without coercion; and second: collecting evidence that they are the real victims.
He explained that once the victim has been authorized, the lawyer has the right to defend only in the case of authorization, that is, can not go to do anything more, so please all victims do not worry.
Mr. Ky Tech added that in the past, Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has been constantly monitoring the latest developments in this case.
He said that in the past, attention has been shown by arresting those involved and ending the function of the duke and is seeking all means to help the victims. He stressed that Leng Channa is currently in prison under strict legal action.
He revealed that the Royal Government has ordered another professional team to search for the property of the faction of former tycoon Leng Channa from the fraud in the past.
