Mr. Bun Chanvannak said this on July 11, 2024, on the occasion of the High Representative, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, inspected, assessed, handed over and completed the period of guarantee on the construction of paved roads from One thin layer (DBST) and one mixed road in Siem Reap.
These two roads include: Construction of a DBST paved road, 3,000 meters long, 6 meters wide, 1 meter wide gravel sidewalk, located in Tram Kang village, Chanlas Dai commune, and Kouk Trom village, Sranal commune, Kralanh district. Siem Reap.
Another 7,000-meter-long and 8-meter-wide gravel road is located in Thkov village, Sen Sok commune, Kork Thmor village, Reul village, Prey Kor commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province, along with the construction of drainage and road signs Will be providing public benefits, especially to the people as a basis for travel and transportation of agricultural products.
