(Phnom Penh): Lok Chumteav Dr. Pich Chanmonin presided over the irrigation ceremony of Sokun Vary to present to His Majesty the King Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat as the Chief Inspector and Monk of Wat Ounalom.
Please be reminded that after the body of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Tep Vong, the former Chief Bishop of Wat Ounalom, he passed away on February 26, 2017, the Board of Directors of the Mahanikaya and the Ministry of Cult and Religion decided to appoint His Royal Highness Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat as the 8th Chief Bishop to lead the popular Royal Monastery on June 24, 2018 (2024). As of BE 2568, Wat Ounalom is 582 years old.
The name Ounalom is derived from the name of a large stupa or ancient temple named Ounalom (eyebrow hair is the hair that grows on the meeting of both eyebrows different from normal eyebrows), which is the burial place of the hair of the Buddha named Assit Chitthar. Located in the pagoda compound today.
The history of the pagoda's chaplain is mostly the honor of the prince who led the pagoda in the past, including Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Nil Teang, Samdech Preah Sangka Reach Chuon Nath, Samdech Preah Sangka Reach Huot Tat and Samdech Preah Moha Sangka Reach Tep Vong, and now there is Samdech Preah Great Noble Family Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat is the 8th Chief Bishop.
He (Samdech Yeat) was born in Battambang province, the son of Disciple Chak Yorn and Disciple Prum Loeut, with seven siblings, of whom he was the second child. He started to build a pagoda in 1991 under the auspices of Venerable Choat Nhano Pankid and completed his training as a monk in the presence of Venerable Tipo Ouk Muth in the border of Wat Kampheng, Battambang Province.
Structure of Wat Ounalom: 1: Samdech Preah Moha Areyvong, Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat, Preah Chao Athikar 2: Preah Dhammakhouchachar Chuon Savoeun, Preah Krou Sothisthum 3: Preah Kitti Thammavong Srey Naron, Preah Kru Soth Chhveng 4: Preah Ind Vongsa Preun Soeun Preah Vinay Thor 5: Preah Kitti Visal Vong Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha Instructs New Provincial Governor to Crack Down on Gambling and Gangs
