(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, July 12, 2024, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, held a meeting with the working group of the Royal Government to assist the capital-province to review the work results.
The Royal Government-Capital Working Group is a mechanism established by the Royal Government to push national officials to assist in local development work with sub-national authorities.
This is the first meeting of the first half of the working group of the Royal Government in the capital and provinces to review the results. From the 5th legislature of the National Assembly, the Royal Government has established a national working group on localization, which is now renamed as the Royal Government Working Group on Capital-Provincial Localization with the following objectives:
1. Promote the dissemination and promotion of the implementation of political programs, strategic frameworks, and reform programs and key measures of the Royal Government. Understand and evaluate the actual situation at the local level 4: Participate in solving practical problems on the spot in a timely and efficient manner to respond to the requests and needs of the people.
The Royal Government considers working on the ground as an important and necessary way of working. Based on the necessity and the good results of the past period, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly decided to continue to maintain the mechanism of the Royal Government working group on the ground and also adjusted the composition in accordance with the actual situation.
In order to strengthen the work of the working group of the Royal Government to help at this base, Samdech Ipti has introduced some of the following work as well.
3. The Royal Government working group at all levels must pay attention to the local level, where each working group is responsible for cooperating and promoting the implementation of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategic Political Program, the six priority policy programs, and Key measures of the Royal Government, as well as strengthening cooperation to promote solutions to meet the challenges of local people in a timely and effective manner.
4. The Royal Government working group at all levels must report on the activities and results of the local work on a regular basis to the Office of the Council of Ministers to summarize the report to the Royal Government.
5: The Office of the Council of Ministers shall introduce the report format for the local government working group, summarize and report on the activities and results of the field visit, and prepare the guidance document for the local government working group, co-organize the public forum to promote the response. Local challenges effectively.
