(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Mang Sineth, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, discussed with the delegation of the Cambodia-Laos Friendship Association led by Mr. Khambai Damlat, Vice President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Member of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party and Chairman. Lao-Cambodia Friendship Association This ceremony was held at the provincial hall on the afternoon of July 11, 2024.
Mr. Mang Sineth described the main areas of the first province. There are three autonomous ports (Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, Stung Hav Port, and Oknha Mong Rithy Port). Allow ships carrying 30,000 to 40,000 tons to dock, that is, more than 70 percent of the country's cargo passes through the port of Sihanoukville.
It is the vision of the Royal Government to develop this port into three phases, the first phase from 2024 to 2027, the second phase from 2025 to 2028 and the third phase, these three phases have a water depth of 14.5. Meters up to 17.5 meters will be able to accommodate ships weighing up to 160,000 tons. He said that after completing these three steps, our autonomous port will be able to receive the traffic of the world's largest ships docked without problems.
He emphasized that the first phase of the project was inaugurated on December 22, 2023 under the presidency of Samdech Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Separately, the provincial airway also has an international airport that is being expanded to become a modern international gateway with more than 3,300 meters of state roads for parking and has a new project, the current new terminal. Construction is scheduled to be completed in 2027.
Turning to tourism, the first half of 2024 has a total of 2.8 million national and international tourists, and most visitors are interested in the islands in the province, because the beaches on those islands are beautiful. Fresh and unique air on the beach in Sihanoukville. In addition, Sihanoukville has 37 infrastructure lines, a main road, and three treatment bases.
