Taxpayers who properly perform their tax obligations will not be on the list of high-risk enterprises for audit purposes.
He added that in order to support taxpayers in fulfilling their tax obligations properly, the General Department of Taxation has taken care to continuously improve the provision of taxpayer services in order to promote the culture of payment. Taxes and strengthen fiscal compliance that will ensure revenue sustainability for the benefit of the national budget in line with the Royal Government's revenue collection strategy.
Mr. Kong Vibol said this through the weekly newsletter of the General Department of Taxation, published on July 11, 2024.
According to the "Manual of Tax Audit Procedures and Procedures for Tax Officers and Taxpayers" in the analysis or irregularities of taxpayers, the tax administration can examine and analyze through the following three methods: Under:
1. General analysis is a preliminary analysis of the overall situation of the enterprise, including the status of filing tax returns, economic or business activities, use of accounting systems or other information available to the tax administration.
2. Analysis of financial statements and tax returns is an analysis using information or data from taxpayers' financial statements and tax returns, focusing on irregularities in the accounts or the proportions of any accounts. Differences between information and data and comments contained in independent audit reports.
3. Ratio analysis is a verification of the ratio of different data that can be extracted from a single financial statement or different financial statements, such as balance sheets and income statements.
