Parliamentary Diplomatic Mission of National Assembly President Khuon Sodary in Thailand for the Prosperity of Villagers, Fences and Global
(Phnom Penh): National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, begins a two-day official visit to the Kingdom of Thailand on July 11, 2024. The visit is aimed at strengthening the cooperation between the two parliaments at both bilateral and multilateral levels, meeting the needs of both peoples and maintaining prosperity for the people of the world. Mr. too.
Cambodia-Thailand relations, which have reached 75 years, were upgraded from a "partnership for peace and prosperity" to a "strategic partnership" in early 2024, during a visit by Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet. In Thailand in February. At the same time, relations and cooperation between the two parliaments have been proudly promoted.
In recent times, the leaders of the two countries have exchanged visits, which has shown a strong will to hide the traditional and long-standing relations between the two countries. More cohesiveness that will bring mutual benefits.
Thailand is the third overseas visit of National Assembly President Khuon Sodary since taking office as Speaker of the National Assembly for the seventh term. The National Assembly President paid a visit to Vietnam and Laos in connection with the first summit of the CLV Regional Assembly President. He then paid a visit to France and attended a meeting of the presidents of the Global Women's Parliament in Paris, hosted by the French National Assembly.
The Overseas Mission of the President of the National Assembly responds to the aspirations of the people in building peace, social prosperity for sustainable development based on the principles of independence, sovereignty, loyalty and mutual benefit. Parliamentary diplomacy will bring people-to-people cooperation closer for the promotion of key areas such as tourism, economy and trade, and to promote the principle of pluralism in the world. Also.
During his visit to Thailand, National Assembly President Khuon Sodary and His Excellency Van Mohammad Namor said that the President of the National Assembly of Thailand will sign a Memorandum of Understanding between the two parliaments to enhance cooperation in all fields. Exchanges of visits from all levels, including leaders, expert committees, friendship groups, women MPs and young MPs.
At the same time, the two secretariats of the National Assembly will also sign a memorandum of understanding to strengthen cooperation in building the capacity of Secretariat officials to provide better services to MPs on missions.
