Norway has already sent two F-16s to Denmark for training for Ukrainian pilots. The decision to supply F-16s to Ukraine was made in August last year, but did not specify the number of aircraft at the time.
Denmark and the Netherlands have also pledged to provide F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine. Denmark has pledged to donate 19 aircraft, while the Netherlands has pledged 24. Both countries have been playing a key role in helping Ukraine resist Russian attacks.
