Ministry of Information spokesman calls on citizen to become anti-fake news
(Phnom Penh): In the context of the rapid development of technology, the number of users of social media has increased due to convenience and speed. At the same time, the distribution and distribution of digital content has also increased significantly, in addition to the official public-private media. For this reason, society has many sources for sharing information, both good and bad, both true and false. This is according to Mr. Tep Asarith, spokesman for the Ministry of Information.
In an interview with Fresh News, a spokesman for the Ministry of Information called on individuals to become opponents of fake news by increasing respect for and implementing the conditions for responsible information users, increasing vigilance and taking action. Pay close attention before deciding to share or disseminate any information to family and others.
In a society that is stable, orderly, and prosperous, it is a society with a secure information space, that is, there is a circulation of factual information from all angles and quality, which is a necessary element to support the people as a basis for making decisions for livelihoods and Daily living.
False information, in particular, can have serious consequences, such as loss of public trust, loss of time, money, or reputation, damage to privacy, or even harm to one's life. In addition, the dangers of false information can cause discrimination, create hostility in society and undermine the assurance of public order, stability and national security.
Under the leadership of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, the Ministry of Information has been playing an important role in maintaining order in the field of information security, information security in Cambodian society by ensuring the access of quality and safe information to the people to contribute to strengthening security and National stability.
Tep Asarith, spokesman for the Ministry of Information, called on all citizens who receive information or users on social media to verify the information they receive before deciding to share or disseminate it. Of information to ensure confidence.
