(Oddar Meanchey): The main canal of Chongkal in Chongkal commune, Chongkal district, 1260 meters long, was rehabilitated by Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to be ready to intervene to rescue rice and other crops of the people when encountered. Drought.
Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, said on the afternoon of July 10, 2024 that following the instructions of Mr. Thor Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology is always active. Regular maintenance of canals as well as other reservoirs in the province to store water for use in the dry season.
The Director of the Department stated that on July 10, 2024, the working group of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology rehabilitated 1 main canal with a length of 1,260 meters to be ready to intervene in case of drought. For irrigating rice and water used in daily life of the people in Chong Kal commune, Chong Kal district.
Mr. Nhen Kuon further stated that the main canal that is being rehabilitated now is the old canal which is in a shallow condition, so the department is working to restore water from Stung Sreng I to supply the Chongkal Reservoir.
He said that in case of water shortage in the dry season and the end of the rainy season, we will continue to pump water to the end of the lake, so we can open the water gate for distribution, and this pool is not only for irrigation, but for supply. Raw water for the production of clean water in the town of Chongkal district.
The director of the department stated that the Chongkal Reservoir is capable of irrigating 393 hectares of dry rice, 1,300 hectares of wet rice and 18 hectares of mixed crops. He said that the main canal is not for irrigation, but this canal It is very important for pumping water to the end pool.
