Senior officials of the Ministry of Rural Development led an inter-ministerial working group to inspect and evaluate the completion of the construction of four roads in Battambang and Siem Reap.
(Siem Reap): Dr. Nuon Danhel, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on July 9-10, 2024, led the Inter-Ministerial Working Group to inspect and evaluate the completion of 4 road construction projects. 3 projects in Battambang and 1 project in Siem Reap.
Project 2: Construction of a 8,000-meter-long, 8-meter-wide paved road from Ma Khluor and Boeung Chum Neang villages, Prey Khpos commune to Orussey village, Boeung Pram commune, Bavel district, Battambang province.
Project 3: Construction of a 4,000-meter-long, 8-meter-wide gravel road from Kbal Spean village, Lvea Chas village and Tani village, Lvea commune to Krope Sesip village, Boeung Pram commune, Bavel district, Battambang province. Street names as well.
Project 4: Construction of a 3,400-meter-long, 7-meter-wide DBST paved road on both sides of the paved road, construction of drainage and road labeling in Tram Kang village, Thlok village, Sleng Spean commune, Srey Snom district, Siem Reap province. All these projects are implemented by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense.
On that occasion, Dr. Nuon Danil praised the constructive efforts of the Department of Engineering of the Ministry of National Defense to achieve the plan and quality, because the construction, rehabilitation, maintenance, as well as the improvement of physical infrastructure is a necessary investment to facilitate. To provide transportation and other public services to people all over the country, which is an important part of improving the living standards and reducing poverty of rural people.
It should be noted that after inspecting the road and sewer project above, Dr. Nuon Danhel and the inter-ministerial working group met with local authorities and people who benefited from the construction of the road and sewer. I urge all local authorities and residents to take care of their local roads and sewers for a long time for the public good, especially for all of them.
During the ceremony, Dr. Nuon Danhel also brought a precious gift from Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development to distribute to the people, each family received one krama.
