ASEAN Secretary-General attends China General Chamber of Commerce's World Entrepreneurship Summit in Hong Kong
In his speech, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized that the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) is an important foundation for a stronger ASEAN-China partnership and encouraged Chinese entrepreneurs to join ASEAN in organizing the page. Exciting new economic cooperation to drive innovation and embrace digitalization.
The ASEAN Secretary-General also met with Sun Yu, Vice President and CEO of the Bank of China in Hong Kong. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ASEAN financial initiatives on digitalization, environment and financial sustainability, as well as exploring possible areas of cooperation to create greater benefits for both peoples.
Separately, on Wednesday afternoon, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, discussed with Mr. Andrew Leung, Chairman of the Legislative Council of Hong Kong. During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on regional economic development and discussed ways to further strengthen economic and people-to-people ties between ASEAN and Hong Kong.
On Wednesday afternoon, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, also discussed with Dr. Ma Jun, President of the Hong Kong Green Finance Association. During the meeting, the two sides discussed ongoing ASEAN financial initiatives on digitalization, environment and financial sustainability, as well as explored possible areas of cooperation.
EHL, one of Switzerland's prestigious higher education institutions, is renowned for its rigorous academic standards and world-class hospitality curriculum. With more than 125 years of history, EHL is considered one of the world's leading hospitality, education, hospitality and service pioneers. Studying at this university costs at least $ 500,000.
