The National Audit Authority has the role of assisting the Royal Government to see whether the use of the budget of all ministries, institutions, departments and units is in accordance with the law and regulations.
(Kep): Dr. Suon Sethy, Deputy Auditor General, Representative of Dr. Som Kimsour, Auditor General of the National Audit Authority, said that the National Audit Authority has an important role to play in helping the Royal Government to see how the budget of the ministries and institutions. All units comply with the law or not.
He said this at the opening ceremony of the seminar on "Law on Audit and Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia" to leaders and civil servants in relevant departments and units, as well as the Armed Forces and city-district and commune leaders. Sangkat of Kep Provincial Administration on July 9, 2024 at Sangkhamit Hotel in Kep Village, Sangkat Kep, Kep City.
Dr. Suon Sethy said that the audit of a subject is not to find fault, but to find points to improve how to be transparent on revenue collection and other expenses. Auditing is a necessary job that requires the relevant professional officers to know the law.
Dr. Prohm Vichet Sophorn, Deputy Secretary General and Lecturer of the National Audit Authority, gave a presentation on "Audit Law and Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia", focusing on three key points:
* First, the purpose of disseminating the law on audit and public audit standards. * Second: Content of the Law on Auditing of the Kingdom of Cambodia. * Third: Content of the Public Audit Standards of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
He stressed that the National Audit Authority conducts independent work in conducting external audits of the Royal Government to strengthen good governance in overseeing the operations and programs of public institutions, making it transparent on revenue collection and expenditure. National budget, monitoring and reviewing the accuracy and appropriateness of financial statements, strengthening the internal control system of public institutions.
