Dhaka: Floods in Bangladesh have swept away homes and forced the closure of schools, forcing tens of thousands of people to flee their homes, and more heavy rain forecasts are expected in the coming days. Expect the situation to get worse. This is according to the release by Reuters on July 9, 2024.
The Ministry of Disaster and Emergency Services says about 40,000 people are seeking asylum in government shelters and more than 600 emergency teams have been set up to treat flood victims.
The floods, caused by heavy monsoon rains, caused severe damage to flooded roads, bridges and dams. Local authorities have warned that heavy rains are likely to continue in the central and southern regions, which could worsen the flood situation.
