General knowledge: Radium and radioactive substances
(Phnom Penh): Radium (Radium) is a metal that causes radiation as it was first discovered in the late 19th century by a couple of scientists, but radium has both advantages and disadvantages due to its radioactive substance. It. Who discovered radiation?
Today, radium is the most valuable metal because to get 2 grams of radium, many tons of ore must be dissolved, while a small piece of radium is worth tens of thousands of dollars because it is a very rare metal. The main benefit of radium is that it can cure skin cancer, tumors and many other skin diseases through its green light.
However, radium was later discovered to be harmful to human health when it was used in various chemical processes due to its high levels of radiation and chemical reactions. Currently, apart from its use in medicine and nuclear, radium is not used in any other field.
