(Phnom Penh): Conservation International Cambodia works in partnership with the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Fisheries Administration, the Department of Environment, development partner authorities, especially local communities, to plant more than 600 hectares of flooded forest in the Tonle Sap area. More than 270,000 trees since its mission in the area since 2010. By 2030, CI Cambodia expects to support the rehabilitation of about 2,660 hectares.
