(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a notification to all national and international media that the coverage of the voter list and voter registration process 2024 All journalists must have a journalist identification card issued by the NEC.
To obtain an identity card, a journalist must apply to register as a journalist directly at the NEC. The application for registration as a national and international journalist with a permanent office in the Kingdom of Cambodia must be accompanied by:
* A copy of a proclamation authorized by the Ministry of Information that is valid * A certificate or letter requesting the registration of a NEC journalist from the relevant unit * A copy of a press card issued by the Ministry of Information or an association or association that is valid Recognized by the Ministry of Information * Curriculum vitae with a photo and 4 x 6 photos for identification * Copy of passport (for foreigners).
According to the NEC, applications for registration as an international journalist without a permanent office in the Kingdom of Cambodia must be accompanied by:
* Copy of passport * Journalist ID card of the unit * Curriculum vitae with photo and 4x6 photos for ID card.
The application for registration as an independent journalist must be accompanied by:
* A copy of the press card issued by the Ministry of Information or the Association of Certified Journalists * Curriculum vitae with photo and 4x6 photos for identification * Last article published in the parallel newspaper Laws during the last year, 3 (three) articles.
