Pursat Provincial Governor Considers It Is Illegal to Provide Administrative Services and Charges Out of OWSO
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, on July 9, 2024, considered that the provision of administrative services and the collection of administrative fees under the jurisdiction of the municipal / district administration and took place outside the gate office. The only one is illegal and must not be allowed to exist during his tenure.
The provincial governor said this at the meeting of the Provincial Council on the occasion of chairing a meeting to monitor and strengthen the implementation of administrative services to the people at the OWSO and the OWSO. All 7 of Pursat province.
Mr. Khoy Rida stated that the OWSO is a one-stop shop for all administrative services in one place in order to improve the quality, efficiency, effectiveness, transparency and accountability of administrative services at the sub-national level and as a service constraint. Administration to be close to the people to make it easier to provide administrative services to the people quickly, timely response to the needs of the people.
He asked the administrative service staff at all levels to absolutely avoid the provision of some services that are delayed, both the provision of public administration services and computer data entry, please check thoroughly and accurately specify the price. Service, service period and validity so that the people have confidence and no prejudice against our leaders.
At the same time, he also announced to take action according to the law without exception for those officials who take fees for public services from the people in excess of the law, especially officials of the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Land / City / District. 7 and 49 commune / sangkat clerks. The same applies to other services such as civil status, family book or ID card, not to be in case of payment, the mayor / district is responsible.
