(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, the 4th day of the month of Asat, the year of Rong Chhasak, BE 2568, which falls on July 9, 2024, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, pays homage to In honor of His Majesty King Yeang, the 29th "Tree Day" celebration was held at the Banteay Angkor Forest Extension and Restoration Station in Khnar village, Lay Bo commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province.
The 29th Tree Day Ceremony, which is currently underway, is located at the Banteay Angkor Forest Promotion and Restoration Station in Khnar Village, Tram Kak District, Takeo Province, next to the Tree Day Plantation, which is revered by His Majesty the King. The Most High was reigned in 2008.
Banteay Angkor Station was established in 1987 by the Takeo Provincial People's Revolutionary Committee and handed over to the current Department of Forestry, Forestry Administration to manage and establish a 1,100-hectare tree planting station.
For the 9th of July 2024 Tree Planting Ceremony, a total of 3,000 saplings of rose and peacock will be planted on this 3-hectare site. In particular, in 2024, the Forestry Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has just completed the planting of 16,500 seedlings on another 10 hectares of land at the Sokrom Forest Extension and Rehabilitation Station in Samrong Commune, Phnom Kravanh District. Pursat Province.
So far this year, the Plant Day Festival has established a total of 475 hectares of day gardens in 14 capitals and provinces, and the Tree Day event has also established a forest-loving movement and planted many other trees throughout the country, establishing plantations. More than 80,000 hectares and many public or private parks in schools, pagodas, resorts and private parks.
The Ministry of Health said that on July 6, 2024, the Ministry of Health issued a press release on the prevention of health problems caused by eating catfish poisoning after seven cases of catfish poisoning in Kampong Chhnang province. Timely rescue.
But on July 7, 2024, a man in Oddar Meanchey province died after eating catfish, and on July 8, 2024, another man in Kampong Chhnang province also died after eating catfish. (This man is not in the previous seven cases).
Therefore, the Ministry of Health, in cooperation with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, would like to call on and remind all citizens to continue their personal vigilance with a high sense of responsibility to avoid crocodile poisoning causing possible health problems. To lose life, people should not eat crocodile fish that are poisonous because the toxins in the fish can cause serious illness or death.
Toxins in catfish can not be eliminated, even when cooked or frozen. In addition, the five venomous catfish are the most toxic during the breeding season, which usually occurs in February, March and between July and September.
When we eat these fish, the toxins penetrate the central nervous system and can cause death. Toxins in the body of fish also have different levels: eggs and their sweetness are the most toxic, followed by liver, intestines, skin and meat.
Symptoms occur after eating such fish for 20 minutes to 2 hours, such as itching in the lips and mouth, then headache, dizziness, itching in the limbs, difficulty speaking, loss of balance, weakness, muscle paralysis. Limbs, vomiting, diarrhea, fatigue, stiff jaw or may cause death. In severe cases, death may result from respiratory failure.
Immediate post-poisoning relief can be achieved by vomiting (if possible), which can help flush out some of the toxins from the body, and the victim must seek immediate medical attention at a health facility. Closest to you due to toxic status requires under close medical supervision.
The Ministry of Health encourages all citizens to follow the above advice and continue to spread this educational message to the family to protect you and your family from getting sick and dying from eating crocodile fish. These 5 types.
