The event is attended by members of the French business community in Cambodia, as well as representatives of French companies in the region who wish to better understand the Cambodian market, representatives from major companies such as construction and infrastructure companies, digital, healthcare. , Energy, urbanization, tourism, leaf logic, transportation, agriculture and agri-food, as well as sustainable development and the environment.
This second business forum will continue to strengthen the Franco-Cambodian economic relationship and be a unique opportunity for companies, professionals and those interested in economic development to explore the many potentials that Cambodia offers. It is also a time to build relationships with strategic partners, political leaders and experts in Cambodia.
The volume of trade between France and Cambodia was 1.363 billion euros in 2023, which is now Cambodia's second largest trading partner in Europe after Germany. French exports to Cambodia in 2023 increased significantly, by 31% compared to 2022, especially in agricultural, food, pharmaceutical and metal products.
