Message from the King on the Occasion of the 7th Anniversary of the Registration of Sambor Prei Kuk as a World Heritage Site
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, extended a royal message on the occasion of the 7th anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site.
The following is the full text of the King's message:
Congratulations! Today marks the 7th anniversary of the inclusion of the Sambor Prei Kuk site in the World Heritage List.
Sambor Prei Kuk was inscribed on the World Heritage List at the 41st Summit of the World Heritage Committee, held on July 2-12, 2017, with 193 member countries and 21 member countries. Permanent.
Achieving the inclusion of this ancient Cambodian temple as a World Heritage Site is not a simple and easy task. Under the high decision and guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has started to prepare documents to request the designation of Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site in 2012.
The application was submitted to UNESCO, headquartered in Paris, France in early 2016. Nine months after the submission of the documents, ICOMOS experts visited and assessed the actual situation at the Sambor Prei Kuk resort and made a number of recommendations to ensure that the application documents are sufficient in accordance with the criteria of UNESCO and the Commission. World Heritage.
The inclusion of Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List is a great achievement for the mission to protect the ancient temples and to promote the cultural heritage of the Khmer people left by their ancestors.
To celebrate the historic day of achievement in the protection of Khmer cultural heritage in this era of peace, the Royal Government has decided to designate July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance Day as a World Heritage Site. .
Please note that Sambor Prei Kuk Temple Resort is located in Sambo Village, Sambo Commune, Prasat Sambo District, Kampong Thom Province, about 30 km north of Stung Sen City. The area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple is large and there are 7 villages in that area. Sambor Prei Kuk resort is divided into large areas: the former capital area on the west side and the temple area on the east side, separated by a stream called Kru Ke.
Sambor Prei Kuk is the former capital of Isanpura of the Chenla Empire between the late 6th and early 7th centuries AD, the work of King Isanvarman I. The temple is built of ancient bricks, inscriptions, water retainers, city walls and other shrines.
Despite the relocation of the capital to Angkor in the 9th century, the Sambor Prei Kuk area remained an important religious center during the Angkorian period, with additional religious structures and the restoration of existing structures for subsequent worship.
The Sambor Prei Kuk temple resort has been built for many generations, highlighting the temples, statues and other works of art and has become a famous historical site in Cambodia today. Your future will be lost if you have an accident! 1 killed, 11 injured in road accidents nationwide July 7
