Floods, landslides kill 14 in Nepal
Heavy rains, landslides and floods have killed at least 14 people in the last 36 hours, officials in Nepal said on Sunday. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
According to Nepalese officials, nine people were also missing after being swept away by floodwaters or buried in landslides, while 12 others were injured and hospitalized.
In Nepal, landslides and floods often kill people during the monsoon season, which usually runs from mid-June to mid-September.
