End the use of the initial valuation service of all real estate appraisal companies by October 1, experts consider to improve the quality of services to be more accurate.
(Phnom Penh): According to the announcement of the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on July 6, 2024, it is confirmed that from October 1, 2024 onwards, the use of the service Preliminary appraisals for all real estate appraisal companies will be completely closed.
The closure of this primary appraisal service is designed to enhance the quality of real estate appraisals to be more accurate and transparent than ever before, especially on bank lending, as well as to strengthen fair competition.
This decision was made after a recent meeting between the Real Estate and Mortgage Regulators (NCPC), the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors and all real estate appraisal companies.
Oknha Nuon Rithy, CEO of KFA, expressed his support for the decision to close down the initial valuation service to protect the financial sector interests related to property valuation before the bank approves loans to its customers.
"We fully support this decision, which from October 1, 2024 onwards, the real estate appraisal will be carried out as an official appraisal report, which must clearly indicate the responsibility of the valuation service provider," he said. .
He said the closure also strengthened the equitable competition of real estate appraisers.
OWSO: Sen Sok District Administration Continues to Pay Attention to Provide Public Services to Citizens After Additional Encouragement from District Governor
The establishment of OWSOs at the municipal, district and khan levels has the following main objectives:
Promote the principles of good governance, reform of the administrative system by expanding the scope of services provided by municipal, district and Khan administrations by concentrating all services within the jurisdiction of municipalities, districts and Khans to provide customers in one place.
* Improve administrative services, reduce corruption and increase people's trust in the administrative system.
* Promote citizen participation in constructive feedback and criticism to improve the performance of the administrative system
* Keep the administration close to the people, make it easier to provide services to the people quickly, efficiently, quality, transparency, timely response to the needs of the people.
