(Phnom Penh): The Electricity Authority of Cambodia has urged the people who install - use solar energy system (solar system) on the roof of the house connected to the national grid, please do not rush to make self-declaration in time in the first year This is to get legitimacy automatically and not charge anything.
The call was made at a briefing on the requirement for all consumers who have installed and used the solar system on the roof without permission to apply for self-declaration on the afternoon of July 6, 2024 at the office. Electricity Authority of Cambodia.
Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, said that the Electricity Authority of Cambodia has issued a notice on December 15, 2023 for users of solar power systems to make a self-declaration at the Electricity Authority of Cambodia to know the number of people. Use from a deployed location and easily manage network power and security management when needed.
The President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia continued that so far, there are only 94 self-employed people / unit, while the number of locations is still very large. Only 94 self-publishers / units are authorized to become legal users of solar panels. For those who have not yet come to self-declaration and who have not yet received permission will face legal issues.
Mr. Yim Viseth continued that seeing this small number, the Electricity Authority of Cambodia issued the second notice on July 4, 2024 to remind users of solar energy systems to hurry. Post. Therefore, those who make self-declarations during this period will automatically receive legal permission.
Consumption that requires users to self-declare is for any system that is installed and connected to the national supply and connection network. He said that about 95 percent of the people who use solar energy are not obligated to pay for this self-declaration.
The President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia said, "If consumers do not come to self-declaration on time in the first year, in the following years there will be a quota for the installation of solar power systems, so those who do self-declaration "This year will automatically be legalized and will not be charged at all."
Mr. Yim Viseth also said that those who use solar energy only for home use or for cooking pots, light bulbs in the house or on the street through the fence, separate water pump, ie under 10 power. KW or 50 amperes do not require self-declaration.
The President of the Electricity Authority continued that for those who want to make a self-declaration, just go to the location of the Electricite du Cambodge branch or the base of any private electricity service nearest or come to the office of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia by filling out the form. They do not require any payment.
Leaders of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and the President of the Electricity Authority confirmed that during this time, the Ministry of Mines and Energy and the Electricity Authority of Cambodia are preparing regulations on the use of solar energy, including payment, ie only for consumers for business. By factories, enterprises or businesses with a power of more than 10 kilowatts or more than 50 amperes.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, explained in detail to solve people's questions about the requirement to go to self-declaration and not to be required to do self-declaration to the solar system on the roof.
He said that about 95 percent of the population in the housing sector is not involved in paying any fees.
"For the average person, almost 90 percent is not affected. He installs solar power within the housing framework is not involved will have to pay anything," he said.
Ty Norin, permanent secretary of state at the Ministry of Mines and Energy, confirmed that the cost of installing solar panels was limited to commercial plants.
Senior official: The need to announce the solar system on the roof to easily manage data, maintain current stability and prevent accidents to electricians (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Tin Norin, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, explained the reasons why it is necessary for all electricity users who have installed and used the solar system on the roof to apply for self-declaration to control the data of the power source. And safety.
This explanation was made on the occasion of Dr. Tin Norin's participation in the press conference on the requirement that all consumers who have installed and used the solar system on the roof without permission, please apply. Prakas prepared by the Electricity Authority of Cambodia on the afternoon of July 6, 2024.
Dr. Ty Norin stated, "How useful is the collection of self-declaration information? I would like to inform that there are two major benefits: first: the management of data on existing power sources in Cambodia and second: security to Prevent accidents to repairers.
Dr. Ty Norin said that the Ministry of Mines and Energy manages all databases of existing electricity sources in Cambodia. He said that there are many sources of electricity, and the collection of self-declaration information is in the interest of information on electricity sources.
In addition, Dr. Tin Norin said that when self-declaration, we can know which locations have a solar power source on the roof and which are connected to the system. Consumers.
Dr. Tin Norin said, "Normally, when we connect in our house, some people say that I connect to my house, why do I need to make self-declaration, but actually forget that when connected to the home system is connected to the system "Supply and that supply system is connected to the national network throughout the country."
According to Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, those who install separate solar power systems (such as solar lights, cooking pots, etc.) that are not connected to the home network, the state electricity grid, are not required. Do the self-declaration.
He said that the ones who have to do the self-declaration are the ones who install the solar power system and connect it to the home network that connects to the state electricity grid. Japanese Foreign Minister and CEO of CMAC hold joint press conference to present the results and support for demining activities in Cambodia (Video inside)
