The Japanese Minister of Foreign Affairs highlighted this during a courtesy call and discussion with Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, July 6, 2024.
During the meeting, the Japanese Foreign Minister expressed her pleasure and considered the opportunity to meet Samdech Techo as a great honor for her. She reminded that she had met Samdech Techo once in 2005.
The Japanese Foreign Minister praised Samdech Techo for playing an important role in building Cambodia-Japan bilateral relations, especially for his great achievements in raising the level of bilateral relations to a higher level.
She is very proud of the close bilateral relations between Cambodia and Japan in all fields. The Japanese Foreign Minister briefed Samdech Techo on her fruitful talks with the Prime Minister, focusing on new cooperation between Cambodia and Japan and on regional and global issues.
She highlighted the importance of the economic sector and expressed a desire to promote Cambodia's economic potential in order to attract more Japanese investment companies to Cambodia.
The Japanese Foreign Minister also mentioned Japan's focus on demining. She expressed her intention to cooperate with Cambodia, which will host the 5th Review Meeting of the Ottawa Convention on 25-29 November 2024 in Siem Reap.
She also informed Samdech Techo that Japan plans to hold an international conference on mine action in Ukraine in Japan in 2025 and requested Cambodia's support. Regarding regional issues, she praised Cambodia and Samdech Techo for their efforts to find a peaceful solution in Myanmar in the past and stressed that Japan attaches importance to ASEAN consensus and continues to support ASEAN in implementing the five-point unanimous agreement. (5PCs) to be effective.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his happiness to the Minister again after the meeting 20 years ago. Samdech Techo also expressed his pleasure at the Minister's visit to Cambodia to review the achievements of bilateral relations and cooperation between the two countries since Japan participated in the peace process in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo stated that Japan has provided a lot of assistance for Cambodia's growth in many areas, from helping to clean water in the city and helping to release water from Phnom Penh, helping to build infrastructure such as Construction of National Road No. 5, National Road No. 1, which is the ASEAN Highway ... etc.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Japanese government for its contribution to Cambodia's economic growth. Samdech Techo has met with a lot of Japanese companies and wants more Japanese companies to invest in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, is very proud to have worked with Japan until achieving a comprehensive strategic partnership in early 2023.
Samdech Techo stressed that Cambodia, despite the change of Prime Minister, Cambodia-Japan relations have not changed, but only to promote this relationship to be even better. Samdech Techo reminded that last January, he went to receive artificial glasses in Tokyo, and on that occasion, the Prime Minister of Japan, Kishida Fumio, warmly welcomed him, even though he is no longer the Prime Minister.
Samdech Techo considered Kishida Fumio an old friend. He also thanked the Prime Minister of Japan for sending a congratulatory message when he became President of the Senate.
Samdech Techo thanked for the results mentioned by the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan in the meeting with Samdech President.
Samdech Techo continued that Cambodia has always supported Japanese initiatives. Cambodia was the first country to support Japan's Free and Open Indo-Pacific Initiative (FOIP) and noted that Cambodia was not far behind Japan in international affairs and in maintaining the interests of peace. Regional stability and development.
Samdech Techo confirmed that Cambodia will participate in the conference on mine action in Ukraine in the field of humanitarian.
Before concluding, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan to convey his greetings to the Prime Minister of Japan Kishida Fumio, President of the Senate and President of the National Assembly. Join hands to strengthen peace and global development under the auspices of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO)
With China as the driving force in safeguarding the fruits of peaceful development, strong ties from the multinational states have joined forces to build the Eurasian political, economic and security organization responsible for the common destiny of mankind.
The leaders of the member states of this regional organization have made significant contributions to global governance through their efforts to maintain security, stability and strengthen global economic development, as well as expand cooperation with observer countries and partners. Dialogue and close cooperation with the United Nations and other regional and international organizations.
