Plant more trees to maintain green cover, protect biodiversity, improve quality of life
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, called on the people of relevant institutions to plant more trees to maintain green cover, protect the ecosystem, biodiversity and provide comfort for living and improve the quality of life. There are improvements.
The provincial governor made this call on the morning of July 6, 2024, when the provincial tree festival was held on July 9 at Hun Neng Primary School in Top Village, Sopheas Commune, Stung Trang District, with the participation of Mr. Khlot Phorn, Team Leader. Provincial councilors, teachers, students, monks and about 500 people.
The governor said that forests are inextricably linked to life on the planet, and that the main causes of natural disasters are largely due to deforestation and degradation. Therefore, we must all work together to the maximum to protect the precious nature in Cambodia by taking care of, protecting and replanting trees as much as possible.
In addition, the forest is an important natural resource to maintain the balance of the environment, which has many functions, such as maintaining water source regulation, protecting the slope, preventing erosion, attracting rain, purifying the air, providing non-timber forest products for use, preserving biodiversity and contributing to National economic development, eco-tourism, ecology, culture and a safe haven for all kinds of animals that live on our planet.
The Provincial Governor appealed to Preah Theranut Thera: All organizations, local authorities at all levels, all educational institutions, monasteries and all citizens to pay attention to the following points:
* First, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Cham Province, Khan Forestry Administration, continues to increase the number of seedlings to serve the above activities and disseminate widely to increase tree planting participation from all walks of life. Year after year, more and more.
* Second: Together, continue to plant more and more good trees of all kinds on vacant land, hills, lowlands, temples, educational institutions, villages and other public places. To increase the fresh green cover in Kampong Cham province.
* Third: For some people who migrate to cut down trees, harvest - non-timber forest products or illegal wildlife hunting, please turn those negative activities to increase agricultural productivity, farming, animal husbandry and other work in Our base, which could be a viable option to minimize the nation's deforestation activities.
Prey Veng Provincial Governor and Indonesian Ambassador Inaugurate Achievements of Cambodia-Indonesia Friendship Primary and Secondary School in Kamchay Mear District
Please be informed that the Indonesian Embassy in Cambodia and members of the Indonesian community in Cambodia have joined forces to rehabilitate the Cambodia-Indonesia Friendship Primary and Secondary School in Prey Veng Province. The two celebrated the 65th anniversary of bilateral diplomatic relations and the 79th anniversary of Indonesia's independence.
The renovation process, which cost more than $ 34,000, includes the supply of new study materials, the supply of laboratories, furniture, bathrooms, reading areas and new school gates. This effort is fully supported by generous donations from Embassy staff and members of the Indonesian community, which today number nearly 100,000.
Ambassador Santo said that the joint efforts of the Indonesian community are a testament to the long-standing friendship between Indonesia and Cambodia. The school was built with funding provided by the Indonesian government in 1995. It has more than 790 students from kindergarten to high school.
Ambassador Santo added that the Indonesian Embassy and the Indonesian community in Cambodia are committed to ensuring that students of the Indonesia-Cambodia Friendship Primary and Secondary School have the necessary materials for their studies. These students are the future of Indonesia-Cambodia cooperation.
Cambodia-Indonesia diplomatic relations were established in 1959 with the signing of a treaty of friendship between the Republic of Indonesia and the Kingdom of Cambodia. Indonesia will celebrate the 79th anniversary of its independence on August 17, 2024.
Mr. Suon Somalin stated that with the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, there have been excellent relations between the two countries over the past seven decades, which have yielded many fruits through the level of communication. High economic relations, people-to-people relations. Also, please celebrate the 79th anniversary (August 17, 1945) of the Indonesian Independence Day.
On that occasion, the Governor would like to thank the philanthropists and the Embassy of Indonesia for donating $ 105,000 for the construction and renovation of the Cambodia-Indonesia Friendship Primary and Secondary School. In the field of education at the local level to grow even more, especially the construction of human resources capable to serve the needs of economic and social development of Cambodia.
