Symptoms occur after eating such fish for 20 minutes to 2 hours, such as itching in the lips and mouth, then headache, dizziness, itching in the limbs, difficulty speaking, loss of balance, weakness, muscle paralysis. Limbs, vomiting, diarrhea, stiffness of the jaw or may cause death. In severe cases, death may result from respiratory distress.
Immediate post-poisoning relief can be achieved by vomiting (if possible), which can help flush out some of the toxins from the body, and the victim must seek immediate medical attention at a health facility. Closest to you due to toxic status requires under close medical supervision.
