The General said that in 2006, Cambodia began to move forward by sending troops to the Republic of Sudan for the first time, and in 2024, during the 18 years of the UN peacekeeping mission, Cambodia sent a total of 9,579 troops in That 818 women went to 10 countries and 12 missions.
General Sem Sovanny added that Cambodia is currently prominent in sending three female commanders to the mission areas, including the Central African Republic, Lebanon and South Sudan.
At the same time, the rate of sending Cambodian women to the mission area was about 17.2 percent, with the general also committed to increasing the number of women soldiers.
