Expert: Southeast Asia is a place of intense strategic competition among the great powers.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that as one of the world's strongest developing regions, Southeast Asia is a place of intense strategic competition among the great powers. Which is a major player in the world economy.
He said that Southeast Asia is a place of intense strategic competition among the great powers, which are strategically located and have long-standing territorial disputes, can attract great powers such as the United States and China to compete in particular. The region is also of global importance in terms of climate change and biodiversity, and Southeast Asia's openness to trade and investment makes it a major player in the global economy.
For nearly 60 years, ASEAN has achieved a lot, thus boosting economic growth. However, ASEAN is facing challenges such as globalization, economic inequality among its members, political stability, democracy, respect for human rights, poverty, global warming, terrorism and transnational crime that have affected development. And local security.
He said that although some member countries such as Laos, Myanmar, Cambodia still do not have strong economic momentum like Singapore, Vietnam, Brunei, these countries continue to strive to expand their economies to catch up with the economies of a number of countries. Also need to learn more about the strategies of countries with high economies, what they do to make their country's economy grow.
He also noted that territorial disputes between the United States and China are still hot in Southeast Asia because of the polar divide of the two powers. He stressed that this was not just a common problem as we know it, there was something deeper that we did not know.
