(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Manet, instructed the Royal Government's working groups to visit the areas affected by the outbreak of pests to destroy the crops of farmers to understand the actual impact.
This instruction was made on the occasion that Samdech Hun Sen presided over the plenary session of the Council of Ministers at the Peace Palace on the morning of July 5, 2024.
In the press release, Samdech Hun Sen instructed the National Committee for Disaster Management, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, local authorities and relevant ministries to strengthen cooperation in intervening to the victims and to consider the need. Of providing assistance such as seeds or other essential resources to affected farmers so that they can resume planting.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet also asked the Royal Government to visit the areas affected by the outbreak of this pest to strengthen the base to understand the actual impact and report and make specific recommendations. To the Royal Government as necessary.
Please be informed that due to the hot weather this year and the prolonged time, the life cycle of the larvae is shorter, the eggs hatch faster, eat more quickly and fertilize faster. Combined with the loss of biodiversity due to climatic factors, the loss of some beneficial species that often play a role in destroying these worms.
The swarms of worms also began to explode in large numbers. So far, many provinces have already reported this problem, as well as adversely affecting many crops.
