(Kampong Thom): On the afternoon of July 4, 2024, Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, and Mr. Pen Vanrith, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and their colleagues intervened to facilitate the distribution of water to more rice fields. 1,200 hectares in Samprouch commune, Stong district, which is experiencing drought and facing damage due to lack of water.
At the same time, Mr. Say Kimlam instructed the local authorities as well as relevant experts to coordinate to monitor all the rice fields of farmers who are facing drought, which lasted for a long time at the beginning of this year, when the rain was not enough to intervene to bring water. Save the rice fields from the pool on September 30 in time.
