(Phnom Penh): Samdech Chao Fah Vor Vong Chey, President of Sri Lanka Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Royal Palace, sent a message of condolences to His Excellency Dr. Hor Namhong, Personal Adviser to the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Lok Chumteav Borey Hor on the death of Hor Nambora, former Ambassador of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the Republic of Indonesia, is his son.
His Royal Highness Prince Kong Sam Ol said in his full condolence message as follows:
Excellencies, Honorary Doctors and Lok Chumteavs! On behalf of the civil servants, staff, workers and police force serving in the Ministry of the Royal Palace, I am deeply saddened to learn of the death of His Excellency Hor Nambora, the son of His Excellency Honorary Doctors and Lok Chumteav on the 3rd. July 2024 at 11:11 am at the age of 64 due to illness.
I would like to express my deepest condolences and share the deepest condolences with His Excellency the Honorary Doctor and Lok Chumteav, as well as all the family and relatives of the deceased.
The death of His Excellency Hor Nambora is the loss of a pious father, a beloved son of the people and an important human resource who actively participated in the cause of national service, religion and The King.
I would like to pay my respects to the late HE Hor Nambora and wish him well. Please accept, Excellency, the assurances of my highest consideration.
