(Siem Reap): Dr. Pon Ladin, Head of Pediatric Cardiac Surgery at Jayavarman VII Hospital or Kantha Bopha, Siem Reap, during a recent press conference, said that Dr. Kantha Bopha has started congenital heart surgery services. Since 2011 with the help of training from foreign doctors.
After two years of training, in 2013, a team of Cambodian doctors began to do all the work on their own, performing surgeries on simple cases up to 8,000 cases of complex and closed ventricles.
The doctor continued that after that, our Cambodian medical team strengthened the ability to perform surgery on children from large to small, with children weighing 2.5 kg, depending on the age of 1 week or 3 days. .
Dr. Pon Ladin said: "Since our first operation from 2011 to now in Siem Reap, Jayavarman VII Hospital, there are 4,000 cases and in Phnom Penh nearly 2,000 cases, so the total heart surgery is more than 6,000 cases and catheterization. "Another 2,000 cases of cardiac surgery, including heart surgery, including catheterization."
In particular, in terms of the mortality rate of children in Kantha Bopha Jayavan VII Hospital, Siem Reap, before 2011, which did not have cardiac surgery services, most of the children who died were suffering from heart disease. For the provision of heart surgery services are provided to both rich and poor, Kantha Bopha Hospital treats all equally.
