Senior official: The Ministry of Tourism and Kampong Cham Provincial Administration is preparing Kampong Cham City as a smoke-free tourism city.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and Administration of Kampong Cham Province is preparing Kampong Cham City as a smoke-free tourism city to reduce the impact of the use of tobacco products and to promote the prestige of Cambodia's tourism as a smoke-free tourism as a clean, green and rich tourism. Security.
To organize this process, the Ministry of Tourism and Kampong Cham Provincial Administration jointly organized a workshop on capacity building to organize Kampong Cham as a smoke-free tourism city under the chairmanship of Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State, Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province. On July 3, 2024.
Mr. Hor Sarun said that Kampong Cham City, as well as Kampong Cham Province as a whole, always pays attention to all areas, especially the prevention of health effects from the use of tobacco products, in which Kampong Cham is also a leading province in Implementing a tobacco control campaign and having received accolades from the World Health Organization.
He added that more importantly, today's workshop highlighted the need for the participation of the Kampong Cham Municipality to make Kampong Cham a smoke-free tourist city.
The establishment of a smoke-free tourism city not only promotes the well-being of tourists and tourism workers, but also contributes to the promotion of public health by reducing the impact of tobacco use on society. Round.
Mr. Hor Sarun, as a member of the Tobacco Products Control Committee of the Ministry of Tourism, strives to engage with the Ministry of Health and other relevant institutions, as well as development partners, to raise awareness of the law on tobacco control. Sub-decrees, proclamations and instructions.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism added that the Ministry has also issued a decision on the implementation of minimum standards on the implementation of a smoke-free environment in the tourism sector, which facilitates all tourism businesses to participate in the implementation of the law on the control of drug products. Brush by simply following the instructions contained in this minimum standard operating procedure.
A midwife at Hun Sen Stung Trang Referral Hospital in Kampong Cham province was disciplined after taking 300,000 riel from a patient with a Health Equity Fund card
(Kampong Cham): The Health Department of Kampong Cham Provincial Administration has issued a press release regarding the case of a midwife working at Hun Sen Stung Trang Referral Hospital who took 300,000 Riels from a female patient to use health services despite having a card. Health Equity Fund.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on July 4, 2024, the working group of the Provincial Department of Health immediately investigated and investigated the case. After the inspection, it was confirmed that this case actually happened as follows:
* First: On June 27, 2024, a 30-year-old woman named Nhem Sokneath was admitted to Stung Trang Referral Hospital for Obstetrics and Gynecology due to a stillbirth (12 weeks old) through an ultrasound examination at a private place. And vaginal bleeding. The midwives then arranged the treatment according to the technique.
* Second: The midwife who treated the woman named above actually took the money, even though she knew she had a health equity fund card.
The Department of Health of the Provincial Administration provides guidance to improve midwives who make mistakes, as well as to implement other disciplinary measures in accordance with the Disciplinary Council in order to learn and improve in accordance with the medical professional ethics.
The team of Stung Trang Referral Hospital and the Department of Health would like to thank the public for the specific information provided to the team to participate in improving the quality of care services of all referral hospitals and health centers in Kampong Cham Province.
