Minister Thor Chetha: Project to expand the irrigation and flood protection capacity of Prek O Damrey Cross-Prek Thmey Irrigation System in Svay Rieng Province Achieved 20%
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on July 4, 2024, accompanied by the leaders and technical officers of the Ministry and Departments, together with Mr. Peng Pursa, Governor of Svay Rieng Province and local authorities inspected the progress. Rehabilitation of Main Canal and Prek O Damrei Crossing of Irrigation and Flood Protection Expansion Project of Prek O Damrey Crossing - Prek Thmey Irrigation System in Kampong Ror District, Svay Rieng Province.
Irrigation and flood protection capacity expansion project of Prek O Damrey Cross-Prek Thmey irrigation system located in the border area of Cambodia-Vietnam in Thmey commune, Reach Mondir commune and Banteay Kraing commune of Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province. So far, the project progress has reached about 20%.
The Minister stated that the development of the O'Damrei Cross-Prek Thmei Irrigation System is aimed at increasing water resources to ensure water safety and security for local irrigation in all seasons, as well as to prevent floods, water supply for Use in people's daily life as a continuous source of water for areas other than the project and serve for use in all areas.
The Minister added that the backs of canals and natural streams will be effective transportation routes for agricultural transport in the region, both by land and water, as well as strengthen resilience to climate change and maintain environmental stability. And ecosystems to promote economic growth, reduce poverty and improve the living standards of people along the Cambodia-Vietnam border.
It should be noted that the project to expand the irrigation capacity and flood protection of Prek O Damrey Cross-Prek Thmey irrigation system to be implemented for 12 months from June 2024 to June 2025 has the potential to increase the irrigated area to about 16,200 hectares and About 3,727 families benefited.
