Unions in Cambodia Demand Central Committee to Publicly Interview Interview Questions and Interviews
(Phnom Penh): Major unions in Cambodia have continued to demand that Central tell the public the questions and unions that have been interviewed, which is the most important element in reporting, which has led to serious criticism.
"We ask Central to present the evidence and we will work together on what is in his report," said Fasali, president of the National Trade Union Confederation, at a press conference on the afternoon of June 28, 2024. "
He added that such unsubstantiated reports were unacceptable as they hurt the country's economy and the tens of thousands of workers expected in the garment and footwear industry.
The president of the National Union of Trade Unions said that so far, Central should show the 14 unions that it has interviewed and researched, if there is, we will be responsible, but if not, what all unions are suing is not wrong.
At the same time, Hang Rary, president of the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, said: "Central should present the questions it interviewed with the local unions because we can not cite a sample with only reports but not enough evidence."
He added that Central's cover-up showed malicious intent to destroy the garment sector and the stability of workers in Cambodia.
In particular, Mr. Sam Soeun, President of the National Council of Trade Unions, said that "Central should dare to present the questionnaire in his interviews with more than 100 workers and dare to show the results of the findings. Ask the workers without hiding.
The president of the National Union of Trade Unions added that Central should dare to show how many negative and positive results he interviewed and how to balance this dark report.
He added that if Central did not disclose the results of interviews with workers it had done, it meant that Central did not dare to take responsibility for what it had done and had bad intentions to destroy the garment sector in Cambodia.
Samdech Thep Hun Manet Recommends 5 Points to Continue to Encourage and Support the Development of Teacher Capacity in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the inauguration of a teacher's dormitory and the awarding of diplomas to student teachers at the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute on the morning of July 4, 2024, Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, made five recommendations to continue Pay attention to and support the development of teacher capacity in Cambodia.
He said that the Royal Government must continue to prioritize the recruitment of both qualified teachers and technical contract teachers, as well as pay attention to meeting the needs of qualified teachers and provide additional resources to support Teacher capacity development and school profile development.
To encourage and pay attention to this important task, Samdech recommends some important recommendations for further implementation as follows:
First, continue to reform teacher training institutions by increasing the qualifications of new teachers and training teachers to improve teacher training to meet the "teacher professional standards", "model pedagogical school standards" and the provision of professional development. Bio on a regular basis.
Second, pay attention to the implementation of new teaching methods, learning methods and assessment methods that can allow students to develop critical thinking skills, solve problems related to daily life, and apply scientific knowledge in daily life. Days.
Third, to enhance the digital qualifications and capabilities of teachers by incorporating the use of technology in teaching and learning, improving digital content, and establishing digital education centers and disseminating digital platforms more broadly and comprehensively.
4.) Encourage the successful pedagogical students to continue to develop their knowledge and professional skills through further study, research, development of technology and digital skills, skill development with stakeholders, counseling and experience. From leadership and collaboration in the workplace and adaptation to the evolving educational environment.
Samdech Thep Dey Hun Manet: To improve the living standard of teachers, not only to increase salaries, but also to reduce the cost of teachers (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Thep Dey Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia The living standard of teachers is not only about raising salaries, but also about reducing costs by providing social security funds for medical treatment and check-ups.
This statement made by Samdech President Hun Manet was made this morning, Thursday, July 4, 2024, on the occasion that Samdech presided over the inauguration of the teacher's dormitory and handed over the diplomas to the students and teachers at Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute.
Samdech Hun Sen Manet continued that the consideration of improving the qualifications of teachers and the professional development of teachers has been clearly set, so the state budget is targeted to expand the education sector in Cambodia. And demand is not enough, which means that demand from day to day increases with the evolution of the actual society.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the definition of a task must have a clear direction, and the Ministry of Education's four indicators to improve the living standards of teachers over the past 10 years have achieved proud results. The reform of teacher training institutions that have been upgraded from the Phnom Penh pedagogical center to a training institute is to increase the qualification level of teachers.
"Consideration of teachers' livelihoods, especially salaries, but addressing salaries is not the only basis for reducing costs by providing social security for health, helping you," he said. Pregnant teachers, we also consider this work.
Samdech Manibodi Hun Manet added that taking into account regional fees and other considerations in addition to teachers' salaries is important. Samdech considered the career as a doctor and teacher to be a high dedication with a clear will to contribute to human life and human resource development, and those who take up the teaching profession are highly committed.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet: Human Capacity is a Determinant for the Development of the Country, Strong People Only Develop Strong (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Nation, because only when people are very capable can a nation be highly developed.
This statement was made by Samdech President Hun Manet on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the teacher's dormitory and handing over the diplomas to the students at the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute on the morning of July 4, 2024.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia emphasized that in order for human resources to be capable, it is necessary to rely on education and training, and the backbone of the education sector, focusing on the quality of teachers, is also a key factor in determining human resource capacity and national development. .
According to Hun Manet, if the teachers are not strong, the graduates will not be good and strong, and the competition will be limited. All this shows that teachers and training institutions are an important factor.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia continues to pay attention to education reform. In this regard, Samdech also praised and appreciated the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, which has set out policies and programs for education reform to ensure the effectiveness and high quality of teacher training in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia noted that at a time when the country was in crisis, the Royal Government's budget was reduced to one of the largest defense sectors, but after the end of the war the budget was reduced to education. Increase. He added that in 2020, the national budget for education was 3.2 trillion riels, and by 2024 it will increase to 3.7 trillion riels.
Please be informed that through the implementation of the reform of the Teacher Training Institute, Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute has strived to develop all forms of hardware and software with the support of the Government of Japan and the people of Japan through the Embassy. Japan to Cambodia and JICA, along with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and other development partners.
Study: Europeans still support Ukraine but disagree on how to end war (Video inside) (Warsaw): A study report released on Wednesday shows that the European Union continues to provide enormous support to Ukraine. To fight the Russian war, but also disagreed on how to end the war. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, July 4, 2024.
The study report was based on public opinion polls in 15 European countries, including Ukraine, and collected data from nearly 20,000 respondents.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet: The Royal Government has no policy to prohibit philanthropists and the community to participate in building schools (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): No, it is only encouraging the community and philanthropists to join the movement to promote education.
This statement was made by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the teacher's dormitory and handing over the diplomas to the students at the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute on the morning of July 4, 2024.
The Prime Minister stated that the Royal Government has no policy to prohibit philanthropists and communities from participating in the construction of schools, but only encourages communities and philanthropists to participate in the movement to promote education.
Samdech continued that in some places, due to the urgent needs of the state, it has not been resolved yet, so the teachers moved with the people to arrange temporary classrooms. Of course, the state builds school buildings every year, but still continues to build schools. Community involvement with the education sector is crucial.
Samdech Hun Sen also instructed the Minister of Education that no matter what the mechanism is, do not restrict parents or guardians to pay only to the school or to the state teachers. But if the community or parents participate voluntarily, do not ban it.
"We have no right to ban parents or philanthropists from helping to develop schools or build achievements in schools," he said.
He added that in the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set many building policies throughout the country for more than 20 to 30 years, including the participation of various philanthropists to support School, too.
