(Siem Reap): Prof. Dr. Khun Leang Chhun, Deputy Director of Jayavarman VII Hospital or Kantha Bopha Siem Reap Hospital in charge of diabetes, said that type 1 diabetes is mostly in older children. Between 4 and 14 years.
He said that the main symptoms that parents or guardians need to know are: eating a lot, losing weight, drinking a lot of water, urinating a lot, fatigue. In case of untimely treatment, the child may faint and if left untreated, the child may die. Therefore, parents and guardians should pay attention to this.
In the last 10 years, there has been an increase of 20 cases a year, he said. This type of disease was found in Kantha Bopha Hospital in both Phnom Penh and Siem Reap, with an increase of 698 people, of which in Kantha Bopha Hospital, Siem Reap Province, there were 309 cases. Most children with the disease are 4-14 years old.
Diabetes is a disease caused by a lack of insulin or the pancreas does not produce enough insulin. The cause of the disease is not yet known.
