Separately, the total number of pedagogical student teachers who received the professional certificate today was 266, 181 females. Among them, 243 undergraduate students (12 + 4), 172 females and 23 trainees (12 + 2), 9 females. This student-teacher successfully graduated in the academic year 2022-2023.
Please be informed that Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute was established on May 22, 2017, which was originally a former Phnom Penh Regional Pedagogical Center and Phnom Penh Pedagogical and Vocational School.
The institute is responsible for training undergraduate teachers in the 12 + 4 system and training teachers for primary and secondary education. In 2022, the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute recognized as a higher education institution with the same status as the General Department.
Through the implementation of the Teacher Training Institute reform, the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute has strived to develop all aspects of both hardware and software, with the support of grants from the Royal Government and the people of Japan through the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia. And JICA, along with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and other development partners.
Simultaneously with the development of hardware, Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute has cooperated with relevant units and development partners to develop software to strengthen the quality of teaching and learning.
As of the 2022-2023 academic year, the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute has completed the training of 418 primary school teachers, 344 females and 472 basic level teachers, 274 females, and provided training programs for trainers. From 67 pedagogical schools, 32 girls.
Currently, a total of 249 pedagogical students are continuing their third year studies, 184 of whom are female.
