Preah Chao Chao Athikar Wat Tek Panha insists on cremation of a child who was electrocuted and dumped in Kampong Tralach district
(Phnom Penh): The body of 13-year-old Sorn Vanna, who was electrocuted by a tuk-tuk selling vegetables for protection against theft, was cremated at the crematorium of Wat Tek Panha, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey on the evening of July 3, 2024.
By Rev. Kosal Vorn Vorn, also known as Mr. Tapak, the pagoda's chief priest is fully responsible for the cost of the sacrifice, in addition to Mr. Sak Kanharith, Governor of Por Sen Chey district. Cambodian homicide investigators, along with Samrong Krom commune authorities, also donated money and food to the boy's family.
Hay Sokhim, chief of Samrong Krom commune, told Fresh News that he saw the hardships of the family of Sorn Vanna, who was electrocuted. Rev. Kosal Vorn Vorn, also known as Mr. Tapak, Chief Preacher of Wat Tek Panha, was very compassionate and donated a coffin worth 350,000 riels, a bag of rice, pure water and full coverage for the cremation.
The commune chief further stated that Mr. Sak Kanharith, Governor of Por Senchey District, donated $ 100 to the family of the deceased through himself. Separately, the investigation team of the murder in Cambodia, after packing the body, also donated $ 100 to the family of the body. Mr. Samrong Krom Sangkat Hall in the local authority also donated rice, water and 100,000 Riels.
Please be informed that the incident happened at more than 12 midnight on July 1, 2024 in Chak Chrouk village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey. And until 11 pm on the same day, the authorities went to check the scene after checking the camera to see the activities as described above.
The woman said that it was only then that she realized that her son had been electrocuted by the owner of the tuk-tuk, and that it was not until about 4 a.m. that he saw the owner of the tricycle dragging his body. Hide it near the lamp post.
Then take it to the back of the house and lift the body, put the tricycle on the tricycle, drive away and escape forever. According to the police, after the incident, the mother of the victim boy filed a complaint and the Samrong Krom Police Station and Po Sen Chey District Police, including the Khan Military Police, conducted a search all night to identify the target and make a series of arrests. But most of the suspects confessed themselves like this.
Telecom Regulator of Cambodia Requests Citizens to Report Illegal Sales, Distribution, Installation or Use of Telecommunication Equipment and Services
This request is made through the notification of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia (TCC) on the import, supply and distribution of equipment and the illegal use of telecommunication services issued on the 3rd of this month. July 2024.
The announcement comes as some individuals have in the past used Internet services provided by Starlink, an unlicensed company to operate and provide internet services in Cambodia, as well as import and distribute counterfeit Internet service providers. And claims to belong to Starlink, which undermines the quality of telecommunications services and public order.
In order to prevent the illegal use of telecommunication equipment and protect the interests of consumers, the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia has reminded the public as follows:
Companies wishing to operate and provide internet services in Cambodia must apply for a license from the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia. All import, supply and distribution of telecommunication equipment must be requested and approved in advance by the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia.
* Individuals who operate and provide internet services without a license from the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia and individuals who import, supply and distribute telecommunication equipment without the permission of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia will be punished in accordance with the Telecommunications Law.
