(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia and First Honorary Vice President of the Cambodian National Council for Women, on this morning, July 3, 2024, authorized a delegation of the National Council of Cambodia. For women, led by Mrs. Kittibandit Ung Kantha Phavi, paid a courtesy call and discussed work at the 7 Makara Palace.
To begin with, Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, expressed his pleasure to meet with the delegation of the National Council of Cambodia for Women, which chaired the annual meeting from 2005 to 2023, except for 2021, which was affected by the Kovid epidemic. 19 which interrupted the annual meeting.
In the field of economy and employment, she reported the progress that women have played in the field of economy and employment, according to the Cambodian Economic Census 2022, showing that 61.8% of women represent the total number of organizations in Cambodia. Most women play leadership roles in small and medium enterprises in selling their products to the market.
According to the survey, women have played an important role in the development of diversified farming communities and production groups, with women leading the development of competent production and business management skills in the community as well as increasing their incomes. Families and communities through non-agricultural occupations and ecotourism services and protected area communities, etc.
Please be informed that before Ms. Kittibandit reported to Samdech the above-mentioned report, she fully declared her support for the Funan Techo Canal Project, which was initiated by Samdech Techo President of the Senate and which the Prime Minister has continued to promote. To be released on August 5, the meeting applauded this historic project.
In response, Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, thanked Ms. Kittibandit, President of the National Council of Cambodia for Women, who reported on the progress and work and praised the efforts of the National Council for Women and related institutions to continue. Jobs are growing further. Samdech Techo also expressed his pride that he personally participated in the National Council for Women in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommended how to strengthen education for women to continue their higher education. He recommended that economic power, combined with the power of knowledge, be strengthened so that the women who are leading as well as the women who are studying continue to have technological knowledge so that they can manage the situation.
Samdech Techo advised to find ways to reduce the gap between women and men, at least at the bachelor's degree level for women to have a higher education to lead better and more successful. Samdech Techo also recommended that a study be conducted on convicted and pregnant women, and especially those with children, asking the Minister of Justice and the Minister of Interior to discuss how to facilitate women. Those.
