Go to school, get a full meal, study under the school feeding program in remote schools, while 300,000 students benefit
(Siem Reap): The School Feeding Program was launched by the World Food Program (WFP) and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports under the auspices of Development Partners, with 64 schools benefiting from 37,500 since 1999.
The program has evolved in line with the socio-economic context, as well as the development of road infrastructure, rural markets and production flows in rural communities, turning from a simple breakfast program to a school feeding program. Using community agriculture as a program has helped motivate farmers to increase cultivation and animal husbandry.
With the availability of breakfast, the students studying at Lvea Primary School expressed their happiness and said that we are happy to have breakfast at Riel School, which helps their families reduce their expenses. In particular, make students full and not dizzy while studying due to hunger.
In order to institutionalize and transform the school feeding program into a complete national program, as well as to ensure the effectiveness and sustainability of the implementation of the National Social Assistance Program, the Royal Government has issued Sub-Decree No. 65 on the implementation of the program. School meals using community agriculture on March 13, 2023.
