The provincial governor said that officials from the Department of Agriculture should advise local authorities in villages and communes not to sign land documents related to flooded forest land. UPDATE: A dead man brought his wife and children to confess, the authorities took the perpetrator to the place where the boy's body was dumped in Kampong Tralach district
(Phnom Penh): A man who listed the power line attached to a tuk-tuk selling vegetables to prevent theft caused a boy to be electrocuted to death at more than 12 midnight on July 1, 2024 in Chak village Pigs in Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey.
After escaping for three days, on the morning of July 3, the perpetrator brought his wife and a daughter to the Samrong Krom Administrative Police Station to plead guilty. The suspect, Ath Chanthoeun, alias Ta Yeak, 54, sells vegetables, while his wife, Som Thou, 52, and their unidentified daughter live in a rented room in the village where the incident took place and are from Thlok village. Ministry of Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province.
The dead boy, 13-year-old Sorn Vanna, had a father named Chhuon Sophal, 43, a construction worker, and a mother, Nuth Sa Mean, 34, a factory worker. He was born in Phsar Lech village, Prek Pnov commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province and lived with his parents in a rented room in the village where the incident took place.
The man said he did not know when the boy was electrocuted. He was found dead at around 4am, but heard that the camera was checked at 12 o'clock at night. As for the word that he bought 4 liters of gasoline, it is not true, he only bought 1 liter for a motorbike, and he did not know the geography of the place where the body was dumped before. But he kept riding, and when he arrived, he saw a quiet place and dropped it off.
