ASEAN-East Asia Economic Research Institute plans to invite Samdech Techo Hun Sen to share experiences of seeking peace and ending war in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): ASEAN-East Asia Economic Research Institute (ERIA) plans to invite Samdech Techo Hun Sen The President of the Senate of Cambodia shares his experience of seeking peace and ending the flames of war in Cambodia.
This intention was confirmed by Professor Tetsuya Watanabe, President of the ASEAN-East Asia Economic Research Institute, during a courtesy call with His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Tuesday afternoon, July 2, 2024.
During the meeting, the professor informed the President about his visit and the ERIA delegation in Cambodia. These include working meetings with the Ministry of Commerce, the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
He informed the President that through this visit, ERIA will continue to strengthen and expand the cooperation between ERIA and the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially ERIA will continue to focus on the framework of cooperation on promoting development. Cambodia, especially on industrial development plans and human resource development in Cambodia.
His Excellency Hun Manet welcomed and expressed his pleasure to meet and discuss with the professors and the delegation on this occasion and highly appreciated the excellent cooperation between ERIA and the Royal Government of Cambodia.
(Kampot): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, urged the Kampot Provincial Information Department to continue its efforts to disseminate more widely so that people can receive more accurate information and understand the policies of the Royal Government, including the development process. Nation, all officials of the Information Department of Kampot Province must continue to fulfill their mission with responsible and professional work, which is the armor of journalists.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra's promotion was made during a meeting with leaders, civil servants, contracted officials of Kampot Provincial Information Department and journalists on the morning of July 2, 2024 at Kampot Provincial Information Department.
Minister Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the Ministry of Information is not just a Ministry of Information Collection and Dissemination, and the Department of Information is not only responsible for retrieving and disseminating information, but must also think about information strategies and policies for the nation.
He stated that there is currently no information policy yet, so in the framework of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate, the Ministry of Information has set the vision is to be a public relations institution of the Royal Government with a proactive and interactive mission. Quality and efficient.
The minister added that the media has played an important role in strengthening people's trust in the government and making the government understand the problems at the grassroots level and bring the government's policies to the grassroots.
At the same time, he said that the role of the Department of Information is the command of the Board of Governors, and the work of public opinion and information is dependent on the officials of the Department of Information, which requires the strengthening of professional capacity to hold. Be stronger and strive to adapt to what is available to increase the efficiency of information work.
At the same time, the Minister said that the press is the fourth power, but in terms of information management, the power of the press is the first power that other powers also need information, if there is no information, the decision can not be That's right.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, on behalf of the First Vice President of the National Committee for Information and Public Coordination, stated that he will continue to seek support from the Provincial Board of Governors to encourage the specialized units to cooperate with the Department of Information in disseminating information on affairs and achievements in the province. Extensive to the people.
He encouraged and encouraged more cooperation between the competent authorities as a source of information and the media, as the authorities and journalists are indispensable partners in the dissemination of information.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra praised and highly appreciated the results of the work done by the Kampot Provincial Information Department, despite the difficulties and shortcomings, but worked together to overcome the accomplishments for the nation and its province, which shows all the dedication to Information and audio-visual sector in the province to develop.
The Minister of Information encouraged all officials by acknowledging the efforts and giving certificates of appreciation to all officials of the Kampot Provincial Information Department.
Mrs. Po Chanraksmey, Director of Kampot Provincial Information Department, made a report on the progress of the work that the provincial government officials have decided to implement in the past and proposed a special action plan to continue to monitor, follow up on false information and respond to false information. Just in time. Continue to manage the media and audio-visual in the province more effectively.
Russey Keo District Governor Instructs the Owners of Plots of Land to Build and Pour Land to Violate O'Veng Canal to Stop and Remove It Immediately
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Bunthoeun, Governor of Russey Keo District, advised all landowners living on both sides of O'Veng Prek to stop pouring soil, encroach on the land of the canal and immediately remove all constructions on the canal land for use. Private and must cooperate with local authorities and competent officials to determine their boundaries properly, otherwise will face legal action.
Mr. Chin Bunthoeun said this on the occasion of leading relevant officials to inspect the location of the Prek O Veng Restoration Machinery to avoid any flooding and to improve the aesthetics in front of Borey Sambath Meas in the village. Boeung Salang, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, on the afternoon of July 2, 2024.
Mr. Chin Bunthoeun, in the process of leading professional officers to inspect the location of the Prek O Veng Rehabilitation Machinery, confirmed that Prek O Veng was encroached upon by the owners of the plots on both sides of the canal and built solid structures on the canal.
According to the district governor, Prek O Veng is 80 meters wide, with a 30-meter-wide body and a 25-meter-wide canal. Restore the canal and facilitate the rapid flow of water and avoid flooding due to rain in five districts of Phnom Penh.
