For a society can thrive because of the increased awareness of the various effects of drugs, traffic laws, gangsters, morality and ethics and become a society with strong human resources, that is, highly educated human resources have Deep thinking and good citizenship.
On the other hand, for people who have a mindset that depends only on what society provides, they always ask what society can help or give me? And in a society with such human resources, it is not really possible to develop a country.
To better understand this issue, I would like to highlight some of the provisions of the Constitution, as well as international conventions and the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, which are recognized and implemented worldwide:
Article 41 of the Constitution states that Cambodian citizens have the right to freedom of expression, freedom of the press, freedom of the press, and freedom of assembly. But no one can abuse this right to the detriment of the honor of others, the good traditions of society, public order and national security. The press regime is determined by law.
Article 19 (3) of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights states that the exercise of the rights set forth in paragraph 2 of this Article requires special duties and responsibilities. Therefore, the exercise of this right may have some restrictions that are strictly limited by law and necessary to: (a) respect the rights and dignity of others, (b) protect national security, public order, health or public morality.
Article 22 (2) of the International Covenant stipulates that the exercise of this right may be restricted only by law and necessary in a democratic society in the interests of national security or public safety, public order, protection of public health or morals or Protect the rights and freedoms of others.
Article 29 (2) of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights states that in exercising their rights and freedoms, all persons shall be limited to the limits set by law in order to ensure the recognition and respect of the rights and freedoms of others. And to properly meet the needs of morality, public order and general well-being in a democratic society.
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday night, July 2, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, showed a video of the first meeting of the National Assembly, first legislature in 1993.
Samdech Techo stated that this video is to summarize the advocacy of the first meeting of the National Assembly on November 18, 1993 of the discussion on the parliamentary budget, or to put it simply, the salary of MPs.
Samdech Techo stated that the discussion lasted for 2 hours and 42 minutes, but asked for a summary of 1 hour and 22 minutes, citing only the opinions of Samdech, Mr. Cham Snguon and Mr. Chhean Won, all three of whom are CPP leaders. Same.
